{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NSZbrFzCTGJD83QTEitjTp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Claims 需要 calibration。Claim 1 从 \"sole driver\" 降级为 \"dominant driver\n2\t  (>95%)\"，\n3\t\n4\t  承认 gradient coupling 有 marginal contribution (~3-5%) 但不改变 practical conclusion。\n5\t\n6\t  C1 表述改为 \"BCE+KL-targets recovers >95% of KL advantage\"，不再用 exact match。\n7\t\n8\t  ARC-c 出现 2-3pp delta，需补充 per-task analysis 解释 reasoning tasks 对 gradient pathway\n9\t  更敏感。\n10\t\n11\t  BCE 30% forced top-k PPL 降至 ~10.0（gap 缩小至 1.2 vs KL 8.82），\n12\t\n13\t  需强化 Pareto frontier 叙事：KL 在 quality-efficiency tradeoff 上仍优但 margin 更小，honest reporting。\n14\t\n15\t  6-point regime curve 基本单调，35% 区间有 ±0.2 noise（单次测量），\n16\t\n17\t  改为 \"approximate phase transition\" 并讨论 single-seed noise source。\n18\t\n19\t  仍冲 EMNLP Main，预期 reviewer avg 3.5-4.0，需 minor revision。\n20\t\n21\t  1-2 位审稿人仍有 incremental concern，但多数认为 empirical contribution sufficient。\n22\t\n23\t  关键防御：C1 causal ablation + 53% mask divergence 是 genuine empirical finding，\n24\t\n25\t  不是 engineering trick。14B MMLU gap 作为 honest limitation 报告。\n26\t\n27\t  '\n28\timagined_experiments:\n29\t- name: Four-condition ablation @ 50% sparsity\n30\t  plan_id: plan_001\n31\t  description: 'Core comparison: KL-only vs BCE-only vs BCE+comp vs KL+comp at 50%\n32\t    model-level sparsity.\n33\t\n34\t    KL-only (5 seeds) as headline, BCE+comp (5 seeds) as primary competitor,\n35\t\n36\t    KL+comp and BCE-only (3 seeds each) as secondary.\n37\t\n38\t    '\n39\t  expected_results:\n40\t    kl_only_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 9.19\n41\t    kl_only_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.04\n42\t    kl_only_hard_mask_ppl_seeds:\n43\t    - 9.21\n44\t    - 9.25\n45\t    - 9.14\n46\t    - 9.19\n47\t    - 9.15\n48\t    kl_only_teal_global_ppl_mean: 11.78\n49\t    kl_only_teal_global_ppl_std: 0.05\n50\t    kl_only_sparsity: 0.498\n51\t    bce_only_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 28.16\n52\t    bce_only_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.21\n53\t    bce_only_teal_global_ppl_mean: 44.05\n54\t    bce_only_sparsity: 0.496\n55\t    bce_comp_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 20.8\n56\t    bce_comp_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.7\n57\t    bce_comp_teal_global_ppl_mean: 25.5\n58\t    bce_comp_compensation_params: 67248128\n59\t    bce_comp_compensation_params_mb: 256\n60\t    bce_comp_recovery_vs_bce_ppl: 2.5\n61\t    kl_comp_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 9.18\n62\t    kl_comp_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.04\n63\t    kl_comp_teal_global_ppl_mean: 11.78\n64\t    kl_comp_recovery_vs_kl_ppl: 0.01\n65\t    kl_comp_compensation_redundant: true\n66\t  result_rationale: \"KL-only 5-seed consistency (std 0.04) 源于 KL loss 的 output-distribution\\\n67\t    \\ supervision \\n为 predictor 提供了强且稳定的梯度信号（SNR ~5.8x BCE）。所有 seeds 收敛到相似的 mask pattern\\n\\\n68\t    因为 KL landscape 有唯一的 well-defined minimum（neuron importance 由 output distribution\\\n69\t    \\ \\n唯一确定）。\\n\\nBCE-only PPL ~28 是因为 BCE 的 factorized gradient 只能学 per-neuron importance，\\n\\\n70\t    无法捕获 neuron interaction patterns。F1 vs magnitude oracle = 0.61 看似不错，\\n但 functional\\\n71\t    \\ quality 差，因为 the wrong 39% neurons 被错误处理。\\n\\nBCE+comp PPL ~20.8 说明 compensation\\\n72\t    \\ MLP 能部分修复 BCE 的 mask error，\\n但不能替代 mask quality 本身。67.2M 参数（256MB）只换来 ~7 PPL\\\n73\t    \\ improvement，\\n且 KL-only 无需 compensation 就已 PPL 9.19，说明 correct mask > brute-force\\\n74\t    \\ compensation。\\n\\nKL+comp ≈ KL-only 因为 KL mask 已经接近 optimal（留下的 neuron set 正是\\\n75\t    \\ \\noutput distribution preservation 所需），compensation 无残余 error 可修复。\\n\"\n76\t  tables:\n77\t  - 'Table 1: Main 4-condition PPL comparison @ 50% sparsity'\n78\t  figures_description:\n79\t  - 'Bar chart: KL-only vs BCE+comp vs TEAL/WINA baselines, PPL on y-axis, conditions\n80\t    on x-axis. Error bars from multi-seed. Key message: KL-only (no comp) outperforms\n81\t    BCE+comp (with 256MB overhead).'\n82\t  analysis: \"Headline: KL-only (PPL 9.19) > BCE+comp (PPL 20.8) by 2.26x, 同时省去 67.2M\\\n83\t    \\ compensation 参数。\\nKL+comp ≈ KL-only 证明 compensation 在 KL 训练下完全冗余。\\nBCE+comp\\\n84\t    \\ 虽优于 BCE-only (20.8 vs 28.16)，但改善仅 7.4 PPL — compensation 是 BCE 的 patch \\n而非根本解决方案。KL\\\n85\t    \\ 对 predictor training 的改进是 structural 的（从 mask quality 层面），\\n不是 compensation\\\n86\t    \\ 能弥补的。\\n\"\n87\t- name: STE baseline (KL + Straight-Through Estimator)\n88\t  plan_id: plan_002\n89\t  description: 'KL loss + STE instead of Gumbel-sigmoid. Isolates loss function vs\n90\t    relaxation method contribution.\n91\t\n92\t    3 seeds.\n93\t\n94\t    '\n95\t  expected_results:\n96\t    ste_hard_mask_ppl_s42: 8.18\n97\t    ste_hard_mask_ppl_s123: 8.25\n98\t    ste_hard_mask_ppl_s456: 8.2\n99\t    ste_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 8.21\n100\t    ste_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.04\n101\t    ste_sparsity: 0.47\n102\t    ste_sparsity_note: Lagrangian slightly weaker, converges to 47% vs target 50%\n103\t    kl_gumbel_ppl_at_same_sparsity: 9.19\n104\t    ste_vs_gumbel_delta: -1.01\n105\t  result_rationale: \"STE PPL 8.18-8.25 < KL Gumbel PPL 9.19，但 STE sparsity 只达 47%\\\n106\t    \\ vs Gumbel 的 50%。\\nLower sparsity 意味着 STE 保留了更多 neurons（实际是更宽松的 task），所以 PPL\\\n107\t    \\ advantage \\n部分来自 lower effective sparsity。核心结论不变：KL loss（无论用 Gumbel 还是 STE 做\\\n108\t    \\ relaxation）\\n都远优于 BCE loss (28.16)，证明 KL loss function 是 advantage 的 primary\\\n109\t    \\ source，\\nGumbel relaxation 只影响 sparsity convergence 效率（不影响 mask quality）。\\n\\\n110\t    STE Lagrangian 更弱因为 STE gradient 是 biased estimator，导致 sparsity constraint \\n\\\n111\t    learning 较慢。\\n\"\n112\t  tables:\n113\t  - 'Table A2: Relaxation method ablation (STE vs Gumbel-sigmoid)'\n114\t  figures_description: []\n115\t  analysis: \"STE 实验确认 KL advantage 来自 loss function 而非 relaxation method。\\nGumbel-sigmoid\\\n116\t    \\ 提供 lower-variance gradient estimates → better Lagrangian convergence → \\nsparsity\\\n117\t    \\ 更准确到达 target。但 mask quality 由 KL loss 的 coupled gradient 决定，\\n与 relaxation 无关。Paper\\\n118\t    \\ 中作为 \\\"R3 concern: Gumbel explains gain\\\" 的直接反驳。\\n\"\n119\t- name: Iso-compute BCE vs KL\n120\t  plan_id: plan_003\n121\t  description: 'BCE training extended to 2700 steps (2.71x KL FLOPs) to rule out compute\n122\t    advantage.\n123\t\n124\t    3 seeds (s42/s123/s456).\n125\t\n126\t    '\n127\t  expected_results:\n128\t    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_s42: 27.97\n129\t    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_s123: 28.06\n130\t    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_s456: 28.35\n131\t    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_mean: 28.13\n132\t    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_std: 0.2\n133\t    bce_isocompute_training_steps: 2700\n134\t    bce_isocompute_flops_ratio_vs_kl: 2.71\n135\t    kl_1000step_ppl: 11.78\n136\t    bce_loss_saturation_step: 500\n137\t    bce_loss_500_to_2700_delta: 0.006\n138\t  result_rationale: \"BCE loss 在 ~500 steps 后饱和（final loss 0.638 → 0.632，delta 仅 0.006），\\n\\\n139\t    额外 2200 steps 几乎无改善。这证明 BCE-KL gap 是 structural mismatch 而非 compute deficit。\\n\\\n140\t    BCE 的 factorized gradient (dL/ds_j depends only on neuron j) 意味着 learning landscape\\\n141\t    \\ \\n存在 fundamental limit — 无论多少 compute 都无法让 BCE 学到 neuron interaction patterns。\\n\\\n142\t    2.71x FLOPs → PPL 28.13 vs KL 11.78 (2.39x gap)，confirmed structural explanation。\\n\"\n143\t  tables:\n144\t  - 'Table A3: Iso-compute comparison'\n145\t  figures_description:\n146\t  - BCE loss curve showing saturation at ~500 steps, with arrow marking KL equivalent\n147\t    compute point.\n148\t  analysis: '完全排除 \"KL wins only because more compute\" concern。\n149\t\n150\t    BCE loss saturation at step 500 意味着 BCE predictor 已到达其 expressiveness limit —\n151\t\n152\t    即使 compute 无限也无法学到 KL-quality masks。\n153\t\n154\t    Gap 2.39x 在 iso-compute 下与 standard compute 下几乎相同 (2.38x)，\n155\t\n156\t    证明额外 compute 对 BCE 无帮助。\n157\t\n158\t    '\n159\t- name: SPON reimplementation on Llama 3.1 8B\n160\t  plan_id: plan_004\n161\t  description: 'Learnable bias vectors + KL training for static correction.\n162\t\n163\t    Recovery rate and interference with dense model.\n164\t\n165\t    '\n166\t  expected_results:\n167\t    spon_sparse_ppl: 8.991\n168\t    kl_pred_ppl_no_spon: 9.217\n169\t    spon_recovery_pct: 7.3\n170\t    spon_ppl_improvement: 0.226\n171\t    dense_with_spon_ppl: 6.182\n172\t    dense_ppl_degradation: 0.065\n173\t    mean_bias_norm: 0.053\n174\t    trainable_params: 458752\n175\t    trainable_pct_of_model: 0.0057\n176\t    teal_with_spon_ppl: 11.79\n177\t    teal_without_spon_ppl: 12.08\n178\t    teal_spon_recovery_pct: 4.8\n179\t  result_rationale: \"SPON 的 static bias correction 只能修复 input-independent 的 systematic\\\n180\t    \\ error。\\nRecovery 7.3% 说明 KL predictor 的 residual error 中只有一小部分是 static bias\\\n181\t    \\ —\\n大部分 error 是 per-input adaptive 的（取决于 specific token context 下的 neuron importance）。\\n\\\n182\t    Dense PPL degradation 0.065 (6.12 → 6.18) 说明 SPON bias 会轻微干扰 dense forward pass，\\n\\\n183\t    因为 bias 是为 sparse activation pattern 优化的，在 dense 下是 noise。\\nSPON 对 TEAL baseline\\\n184\t    \\ 的 recovery (4.8%) 更低，因为 TEAL 的 error 更分散（per-layer \\nmagnitude 误差），static correction\\\n185\t    \\ 更无效。\\n\"\n186\t  tables:\n187\t  - 'Table A1: SPON analysis — recovery rate and dense degradation'\n188\t  figures_description: []\n189\t  analysis: \"SPON recovery 仅 7.3% 直接支撑 Claim 2：static correction 太弱，无法 complement\\\n190\t    \\ KL。\\n同时，SPON 的 dense degradation (0.065 PPL) 意味着实际 net benefit 更小。\\nConclusion:\\\n191\t    \\ SPON addresses the wrong error component — KL's residual is dominated by \\n\\\n192\t    per-input adaptive errors that static bias cannot fix。\\n\"\n193\t- name: SPON subsumption logit-space analysis\n194\t  plan_id: plan_005\n195\t  description: 'Output-space decomposition: linearity test, magnitude ratio, cosine\n196\t    similarity.\n197\t\n198\t    Per-layer orthogonality analysis. 50 samples × 2048 tokens.\n199\t\n200\t    '\n201\t  expected_results:\n202\t    linearity_ratio: 0.264\n203\t    linearity_ratio_std: 0.007\n204\t    magnitude_ratio_spon_vs_kl: 0.158\n205\t    magnitude_ratio_std: 0.009\n206\t    cosine_similarity_mean: 0.196\n207\t    cosine_similarity_std: 0.027\n208\t    kl_predictor_effect_norm: 482.65\n209\t    spon_correction_norm: 76.2\n210\t    interaction_norm: 147.74\n211\t    per_layer_cosine_max: 0.0\n212\t    conclusion_type: weak_subsumption\n213\t  result_rationale: \"Cosine similarity 0.196 (接近 orthogonal，远低于 0.5) 证明 SPON correction\\\n214\t    \\ 和 KL predictor \\neffect 作用在 logit space 的几乎正交方向。Magnitude ratio 15.8% 说明即使 SPON\\\n215\t    \\ 和 KL \\n方向一致，SPON 的修正幅度也只有 KL 的 1/6。\\nPer-layer cosine ≤ 0 (所有层) 意味着在每一层 SPON\\\n216\t    \\ 要么和 KL 正交要么轻微反向。\\nInteraction term 147.74 (30.6% of KL effect) 看似不小，但这是 nonlinear\\\n217\t    \\ cross-layer \\ninteraction — SPON bias 会改变 subsequent layers 的 input distribution，\\n\\\n218\t    但这种 interaction 并不 translate to PPL improvement（SPON recovery 仅 7.3%）。\\nConclusion:\\\n219\t    \\ SPON 和 KL 靶向不同的 error components，且 SPON 的 component 太弱，\\ncomposition 无实际收益。\\n\"\n220\t  tables:\n221\t  - 'Table A1: SPON subsumption metrics'\n222\t  figures_description:\n223\t  - Per-layer cosine similarity heatmap showing near-zero or negative values across\n224\t    all 32 layers.\n225\t  analysis: 'Logit-space decomposition 提供 Claim 2 的 mechanistic explanation：\n226\t\n227\t    KL 的 coupled gradient 学到的 mask pattern 在 output space 产生 large-magnitude correction\n228\t    (482.65)，\n229\t\n230\t    SPON 的 static bias 产生 small near-orthogonal correction (76.2)。\n231\t\n232\t    两者靶向的 error mode 不同（per-input vs static），\n233\t\n234\t    SPON 的 mode 太弱无法 complement KL。\n235\t\n236\t    '\n237\t- name: Training-free baselines (TEAL, WINA, R-Sparse)\n238\t  plan_id: plan_006\n239\t  description: 'TEAL (magnitude + greedy), WINA (weight-informed), R-Sparse (rank-aware)\n240\t    at 30%/50%/70%.\n241\t\n242\t    '\n243\t  expected_results:\n244\t    teal_global_ppl_30: 10.97\n245\t    teal_global_ppl_50: 23.31\n246\t    teal_global_ppl_70: 100.11\n247\t    wina_global_ppl_30: 11.45\n248\t    wina_global_ppl_50: 27.93\n249\t    wina_global_ppl_70: 137.24\n250\t    rsparse_global_ppl_50: 151.2\n251\t    dense_ppl: 6.12\n252\t    teal_greedy_allocation_ppl_50: 33.47\n253\t  result_rationale: \"Training-free methods 的 PPL 随 sparsity 急剧增长（TEAL 30%→50%→70%:\\\n254\t    \\ 10.97→23.31→100.11），\\n因为 magnitude-based pruning 在 high sparsity 下 increasingly\\\n255\t    \\ 删除 functionally important neurons。\\nTEAL > WINA > R-Sparse 因为 TEAL 的 global\\\n256\t    \\ allocation 比 WINA 的 weight-informed scoring \\n更有效地分配 per-layer sparsity budget。R-Sparse\\\n257\t    \\ 的 rank-aware scoring 在 SwiGLU architecture \\n上表现最差，因为 SwiGLU 的 gating mechanism\\\n258\t    \\ 使得 rank-based importance 不可靠。\\nTEAL greedy allocation (33.47) 远差于 global (23.31)，说明\\\n259\t    \\ allocation strategy \\n对 training-free methods 同样重要。\\n\"\n260\t  tables:\n261\t  - 'Table 1: Training-free baselines row in main comparison table'\n262\t  figures_description:\n263\t  - PPL vs sparsity curve for all training-free methods, showing exponential degradation.\n264\t  analysis: \"三层 hierarchy 成立：training-free (TEAL 10.97-100.11) < static-learned (SPON)\\\n265\t    \\ < \\ncontextual-learned (KL 8.82-11.78)。\\nTEAL 作为 strongest training-free baseline\\\n266\t    \\ 仍比 KL 30% 差 2.15 PPL (10.97 vs 8.82)。\\nAt 50%, gap expands to 11.53 PPL (23.31\\\n267\t    \\ vs 11.78)。\\nNon-linear gap expansion 说明 learned contextual prediction 在 high\\\n268\t    \\ sparsity 下 advantage 更大。\\n\"\n269\t- name: Full benchmark evaluation + Pareto frontier\n270\t  plan_id: plan_007\n271\t  description: 'WikiText-2 PPL + 4 downstream tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K)\n272\t    across all conditions.\n273\t\n274\t    Wall-clock profiling. Efficiency-accuracy Pareto frontier.\n275\t\n276\t    '\n277\t  expected_results:\n278\t    dense_ppl: 6.12\n279\t    dense_arc_c: 0.583\n280\t    dense_wg: 0.781\n281\t    dense_mmlu: 0.653\n282\t    dense_gsm8k: 0.488\n283\t    kl30u_ppl_mean: 8.82\n284\t    kl30u_ppl_std: 0.01\n285\t    kl30u_arc_c_mean: 0.443\n286\t    kl30u_arc_c_std: 0.032\n287\t    kl30u_wg_mean: 0.692\n288\t    kl30u_wg_std: 0.006\n289\t    kl30u_mmlu_mean: 0.385\n290\t    kl30u_mmlu_std: 0.018\n291\t    kl30u_gsm8k_mean: 0.072\n292\t    kl30u_gsm8k_std: 0.002\n293\t    kl50g_ppl_mean: 11.78\n294\t    kl50g_arc_c_mean: 0.343\n295\t    kl50g_wg_mean: 0.631\n296\t    kl50g_mmlu_mean: 0.281\n297\t    kl50g_gsm8k_mean: 0.021\n298\t    teal30_ppl: 10.97\n299\t    teal30_arc_c: 0.423\n300\t    teal30_wg: 0.661\n301\t    teal30_mmlu: 0.386\n302\t    teal30_gsm8k: 0.079\n303\t    teal50_ppl: 23.31\n304\t    teal50_arc_c: 0.284\n305\t    teal50_wg: 0.53\n306\t    teal50_mmlu: 0.283\n307\t    teal50_gsm8k: 0.011\n308\t    bce_iso_teal_ppl_mean: 28.13\n309\t    bce_iso_arc_c_mean: 0.265\n310\t    bce_iso_wg_mean: 0.518\n311\t    bce_iso_mmlu_mean: 0.261\n312\t    bce_iso_gsm8k_mean: 0.021\n313\t    dense_latency_ms: 119.1\n314\t    kl30_latency_ms: 126.6\n315\t    kl50_latency_ms: 126.8\n316\t    predictor_overhead_ms: 3.17\n317\t    predictor_overhead_pct: 2.7\n318\t    theoretical_flops_speedup_30pct: 1.36\n319\t    theoretical_flops_speedup_50pct: 2.45\n320\t    actual_wallclock_speedup_30pct: 0.94\n321\t    no_sparse_kernel_note: No wall-clock speedup without custom sparse GEMV kernels\n322\t  result_rationale: \"KL 30% uniform 是 recommended operating point 的 median-tier 表现：\\n\\\n323\t    - PPL: 8.82 vs TEAL 10.97 (−19.6%)，KL clearly wins\\n- MMLU: 38.5% vs TEAL 38.6%\\\n324\t    \\ — essentially tied. Median 下 MMLU advantage 被 seed variance (std 1.8%) 淹没\\n\\\n325\t    - WinoGrande: 69.2% vs 66.1% — KL wins by +3.1pp，超过 noise margin\\n- ARC-c: 44.3%\\\n326\t    \\ vs 42.3% — KL slightly better (+2.0pp) 但 seed std 3.2% 使得 significance 不确定\\n\\\n327\t    - GSM8K: 7.2% vs 7.9% — TEAL slightly better by 0.7pp，within noise\\n\\nDownstream\\\n328\t    \\ advantage 不如 PPL advantage 一致，因为 discriminative tasks 对 specific \\nneuron subsets\\\n329\t    \\ 敏感（不同 seed 的 mask 在 critical task-relevant neurons 上有差异）。\\nPPL 是 average over\\\n330\t    \\ all tokens，对 mask quality 更敏感也更稳定。\\n\\nLatency: 无 wall-clock speedup 因为 standard\\\n331\t    \\ PyTorch 不支持 structured sparse GEMV。\\nPredictor overhead 2.7% (3.17ms/119.1ms)\\\n332\t    \\ 在 sparse kernel 可用时可被 sparsity savings \\n(theoretical 1.36x at 30%) 覆盖。Paper\\\n333\t    \\ 报告 theoretical FLOPs savings + overhead。\\n\"\n334\t  tables:\n335\t  - 'Table 2: Downstream benchmarks across all conditions'\n336\t  - 'Table 6: Latency profiling and efficiency analysis'\n337\t  figures_description:\n338\t  - 'Pareto frontier: x-axis = theoretical FLOPs (or predictor params), y-axis = WikiText-2\n339\t    PPL. KL 30% uniform dominates the frontier. TEAL/WINA/BCE on suboptimal side.'\n340\t  - 'Radar chart or grouped bar: downstream task retention (% of dense) by condition.'\n341\t  analysis: \"Pareto frontier 叙事在 median 下需 calibration：\\n- PPL: KL clearly dominates\\\n342\t    \\ (−19.6% at 30%)\\n- Downstream: mixed. KL 30% uniform beats TEAL on WG (+3.1pp)\\\n343\t    \\ and ARC-c (+2.0pp)，\\n  但 MMLU 平局且 GSM8K 略输 (−0.7pp)\\n- Honest framing: \\\"KL\\\n344\t    \\ dominates PPL frontier and provides comparable-to-better downstream,\\n  with\\\n345\t    \\ advantage concentrated on WG and ARC-c; GSM8K within noise\\\"\\n- Latency limitation:\\\n346\t    \\ 需 custom sparse kernels 才能实现 wall-clock speedup。\\n  Report theoretical FLOPs\\\n347\t    \\ + predictor overhead，acknowledge practical speedup pending。\\n\"\n348\t- name: Sparsity regime analysis (30%/40%/50%/70%)\n349\t  plan_id: plan_008\n350\t  description: 'KL-only at 30%/50%/70% + intermediate points (40%). Test scaling trend.\n351\t\n352\t    Combined with dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt for 6-point curve.\n353\t\n354\t    '\n355\t  expected_results:\n356\t    kl_30_uniform_ppl: 8.82\n357\t    kl_30_uniform_mmlu: 0.406\n358\t    kl_40_global_ppl: 10.12\n359\t    kl_40_global_mmlu: 0.381\n360\t    kl_50_global_ppl: 11.78\n361\t    kl_50_global_mmlu: 0.281\n362\t    kl_50_uniform_ppl: 11.94\n363\t    kl_50_uniform_mmlu: 0.278\n364\t    kl_70_global_ppl: 17.91\n365\t    kl_70_downstream_collapsed: true\n366\t    teal_30_ppl: 10.97\n367\t    teal_50_ppl: 23.31\n368\t    teal_70_ppl: 100.11\n369\t    kl_teal_gap_30: 2.15\n370\t    kl_teal_gap_50: 11.53\n371\t    kl_teal_gap_70: 82.2\n372\t    regime_budget_surplus_boundary: 0.3\n373\t    regime_capacity_cliff_boundary: 0.5\n374\t    ppl_nonmonotonicity: 40% PPL (8.36) < 30% PPL (8.82) under uniform allocation\n375\t      (non-monotonic)\n376\t    downstream_strictly_monotonic: true\n377\t  result_rationale: \"三个 regime 的 mechanistic explanation：\\n\\n(1) Budget-surplus (≤30%):\\\n378\t    \\ 每层都有充足的 neuron budget，uniform allocation 消除 \\nlayer starvation（σ_MMLU 从 9.5pp\\\n379\t    \\ 降到 1.3pp）。KL mask quality 优势最大化，\\n因为 abundant budget 允许 KL 选择 truly important\\\n380\t    \\ neurons 而非被迫 compromise。\\n\\n(2) Budget-constrained (~40%): uniform 反而不如 global（MMLU\\\n381\t    \\ 30.7% vs 38.1%）。\\n当 budget 紧张时，learned per-layer allocation (global topk) 比\\\n382\t    \\ blind uniformity \\n更能将有限 budget 分配给 critical layers。这是 non-monotonic allocation\\\n383\t    \\ preference \\n的机制原因。\\n\\n(3) Capacity-cliff (≥50%): 模型 capacity 本身不足，无论如何分配都 collapse。\\n\\\n384\t    MMLU ≈ 28% ≈ random（4-choice）。KL 仍能维持 PPL 11.78，因为 PPL 是 continuous metric \\n\\\n385\t    更 robust to partial capacity loss，而 MMLU 需要 discrete reasoning chain 完整。\\n\\nPPL\\\n386\t    \\ non-monotonicity (40% < 30% under uniform): 因为 40% 用了 global allocation \\n(10.12)\\\n387\t    \\ 而 30% 用了 uniform (8.82)，但如果比较 30% global (8.98) vs 40% global (10.12)，\\nPPL\\\n388\t    \\ 仍然单调递增。Non-monotonicity 只在 cross-allocation comparison 下出现。\\n\"\n389\t  tables:\n390\t  - 'Table 4: Three-regime sparsity analysis'\n391\t  figures_description:\n392\t  - PPL vs sparsity curve (KL vs TEAL) showing diverging gap at high sparsity.\n393\t  - 'Downstream task retention heatmap: tasks × sparsity levels, color = % of dense.'\n394\t  analysis: 'Regime analysis 的 median narrative：三个 regime 存在且 boundaries 明确，\n395\t\n396\t    non-monotonic allocation preference 是 genuine finding。\n397\t\n398\t    Practical recommendation: 30% sparsity + uniform allocation for deployment。\n399\t\n400\t    KL gap over TEAL grows nonlinearly (2.15 → 11.53 → 82.20)，\n401\t\n402\t    说明 learned contextual prediction 的 value 随 sparsity 急剧增加。\n403\t\n404\t    '\n405\t- name: Mistral-7B-v0.3 cross-architecture validation\n406\t  plan_id: plan_009\n407\t  description: 'KL-only at 30%/50%/70% on Mistral-7B-v0.3 (GQA + sliding window attention).\n408\t\n409\t    Validates that KL advantage transfers across architectures.\n410\t\n411\t    '\n412\t  expected_results:\n413\t    mistral_dense_ppl: 5.52\n414\t    mistral_dense_arc_c: 0.602\n415\t    mistral_dense_wg: 0.787\n416\t    mistral_dense_mmlu: 0.624\n417\t    mistral_dense_gsm8k: 0.365\n418\t    mistral_kl30_teal_ppl: 6.77\n419\t    mistral_kl30_ppl_ratio: 1.23\n420\t    mistral_kl50_teal_ppl: 8.65\n421\t    mistral_kl50_arc_c: 0.318\n422\t    mistral_kl50_wg: 0.629\n423\t    mistral_kl50_mmlu: 0.23\n424\t    mistral_kl50_gsm8k: 0.021\n425\t    mistral_kl50_mmlu_retention: 0.368\n426\t    mistral_kl70_teal_ppl: 13.33\n427\t    mistral_teal30_ppl: 8.38\n428\t    mistral_teal50_ppl: 18.31\n429\t    mistral_teal70_ppl: 61.72\n430\t    mistral_kl_teal_ratio_30: 1.24\n431\t    mistral_kl_teal_ratio_50: 2.12\n432\t    mistral_kl_teal_ratio_70: 4.63\n433\t    llama_kl_teal_ratio_30: 1.24\n434\t    llama_kl_teal_ratio_50: 1.98\n435\t    llama_kl_teal_ratio_70: 5.59\n436\t    cross_arch_ratio_consistent: true\n437\t  result_rationale: \"KL advantage ratio (KL_teal / TEAL) 在 Mistral 上与 Llama 高度一致：\\n\\\n438\t    30%: 1.24 vs 1.24, 50%: 2.12 vs 1.98, 70%: 4.63 vs 5.59。\\n这说明 KL distillation\\\n439\t    \\ 的 advantage 来自 SwiGLU architecture 的通用特性\\n（coupled gradient captures neuron\\\n440\t    \\ interaction patterns），而非 specific model weights。\\n\\nMistral 的 GQA + sliding\\\n441\t    \\ window attention 不影响 FFN sparsity prediction，\\n因为 predictor 只在 FFN block 内操作（input\\\n442\t    \\ = hidden state after attention）。\\nAttention mechanism 差异只影响 hidden state distribution，不改变\\\n443\t    \\ KL vs BCE 的 \\nfundamental learning dynamics。\\n\\nDownstream 在 50%: MMLU 23.0%\\\n444\t    \\ 同样 collapse 到 near-random，\\n与 Llama 的 28.1% 一致（both ≈ random 25%）。\\n这 cross-validates\\\n445\t    \\ capacity cliff 存在于 both architectures。\\n\"\n446\t  tables:\n447\t  - 'Table 5: Cross-architecture generalization (Mistral-7B)'\n448\t  figures_description:\n449\t  - 'KL/TEAL PPL ratio comparison: Llama vs Mistral at 30%/50%/70%, showing consistent\n450\t    advantage.'\n451\t  analysis: 'Cross-architecture validation 成功：KL advantage ratio 在 Mistral 上 preserved。\n452\t\n453\t    GSM8K 的 catastrophic drop (36.5% dense → 2.1% KL 50%) 在 Mistral 上更严重，\n454\t\n455\t    可能因为 Mistral 的 math capability 本身较弱 (36.5% vs Llama''s 48.8%)。\n456\t\n457\t    Limitation: 仍是 7-8B scale，14B (Qwen) 已知有 MMLU disconnect。\n458\t\n459\t    '\n460\t- name: LongBench English subset evaluation\n461\t  plan_id: plan_010\n462\t  description: 'LongBench English subset (4K-32K tokens). KL-only, BCE, TEAL, SPON\n463\t    conditions.\n464\t\n465\t    Per-task-type breakdown. Tests predictor generalization beyond 2048 training length.\n466\t\n467\t    '\n468\t  expected_results:\n469\t    dense_narrativeqa: 18.2\n470\t    dense_qasper: 27.5\n471\t    dense_hotpotqa: 25.8\n472\t    dense_gov_report: 30.0\n473\t    dense_multi_news: 25.1\n474\t    dense_triviaqa: 82.0\n475\t    kl30u_narrativeqa: 12.5\n476\t    kl30u_qasper: 19.8\n477\t    kl30u_hotpotqa: 15.2\n478\t    kl30u_gov_report: 22.1\n479\t    kl30u_multi_news: 17.5\n480\t    kl30u_triviaqa: 56.8\n481\t    kl30u_avg_retention: 0.64\n482\t    kl50g_narrativeqa: 6.2\n483\t    kl50g_qasper: 10.8\n484\t    kl50g_hotpotqa: 7.5\n485\t    kl50g_gov_report: 14.2\n486\t    kl50g_multi_news: 9.1\n487\t    kl50g_triviaqa: 32.5\n488\t    kl50g_avg_retention: 0.35\n489\t    teal30_narrativeqa: 10.8\n490\t    teal30_qasper: 17.2\n491\t    teal30_hotpotqa: 13.0\n492\t    teal30_gov_report: 19.5\n493\t    teal30_multi_news: 14.8\n494\t    teal30_triviaqa: 50.2\n495\t    teal30_avg_retention: 0.56\n496\t    kl30u_retention_4k: 0.72\n497\t    kl30u_retention_8k: 0.63\n498\t    kl30u_retention_16k: 0.52\n499\t    kl30u_retention_32k: 0.41\n500\t    length_degradation_note: Predictor trained on 2048 tokens; generalization degrades\n501\t      with context length\n502\t  result_rationale: \"Predictor 在 2048 token 上训练，对 longer context 的 generalization\\\n503\t    \\ 有 length-dependent degradation。\\n原因：neuron importance distribution 随 context\\\n504\t    \\ length 变化——longer context 中 attention pattern\\n更 distributed，导致 hidden state\\\n505\t    \\ 的 distributional shift。Predictor 学到的 importance pattern \\n基于 short-context hidden\\\n506\t    \\ states，在 long-context 下 partially misaligned。\\n\\nKL 30% 平均 retention 64% 优于\\\n507\t    \\ TEAL 30% 的 56%，说明 KL mask quality advantage 在 \\nlong-context 下 preserved（虽然\\\n508\t    \\ absolute performance 下降）。\\n\\nPer-task-type pattern: extraction tasks (TriviaQA,\\\n509\t    \\ HotpotQA) 受 sparsity 影响较小，\\ngeneration tasks (NarrativeQA, MultiNews) 影响较大——generation\\\n510\t    \\ 需要更完整的 capacity \\n来 maintain fluency and coherence over long outputs。\\n\\nSummarization\\\n511\t    \\ (GovReport) intermediate: 需要 comprehension (robust) + generation (fragile)。\\n\\\n512\t    \\nInfrastructure 风险：基于 registry 中多次 LongBench 失败 (v1-v5)，median 预期 \\n只有部分 tasks\\\n513\t    \\ 产出可靠结果，可能需要 partial reporting。\\n\"\n514\t  tables:\n515\t  - 'Table A5: LongBench results (English subset)'\n516\t  figures_description:\n517\t  - 'Retention vs context length curve: showing degradation from 4K to 32K for KL\n518\t    30% vs TEAL 30%.'\n519\t  analysis: 'LongBench 在 median tier 下提供 mixed evidence：\n520\t\n521\t    - KL > TEAL on all task types（advantage preserved）\n522\t\n523\t    - 但 absolute retention 在 long context 下显著下降（72% at 4K → 41% at 32K for KL 30%）\n524\t\n525\t    - 这 motivates future work on long-context-aware predictor training\n526\t\n527\t    - Paper 中作为 partial success + honest limitation 报告。\n528\t\n529\t    - Infrastructure issues 可能导致只报告 subset of tasks。\n530\t\n531\t    '\n532\t- name: MT-Bench multi-turn evaluation\n533\t  plan_id: plan_011\n534\t  description: '80 multi-turn questions, 8 categories, GPT-4o judge.\n535\t\n536\t    Tests instruction-following quality under sparsity.\n537\t\n538\t    '\n539\t  expected_results:\n540\t    dense_mtbench_avg: 6.35\n541\t    dense_writing: 7.2\n542\t    dense_roleplay: 7.0\n543\t    dense_reasoning: 5.8\n544\t    dense_math: 4.5\n545\t    dense_coding: 5.2\n546\t    dense_extraction: 7.5\n547\t    dense_stem: 6.8\n548\t    dense_humanities: 6.8\n549\t    kl30u_mtbench_avg: 5.15\n550\t    kl30u_writing: 6.0\n551\t    kl30u_roleplay: 5.8\n552\t    kl30u_reasoning: 4.2\n553\t    kl30u_math: 2.8\n554\t    kl30u_coding: 3.5\n555\t    kl30u_extraction: 6.5\n556\t    kl30u_stem: 5.5\n557\t    kl30u_humanities: 5.9\n558\t    kl30u_retention_avg: 0.81\n559\t    kl50g_mtbench_avg: 3.4\n560\t    kl50g_writing: 4.2\n561\t    kl50g_roleplay: 3.8\n562\t    kl50g_reasoning: 2.5\n563\t    kl50g_math: 1.5\n564\t    kl50g_coding: 2.0\n565\t    kl50g_extraction: 5.0\n566\t    kl50g_stem: 3.5\n567\t    kl50g_humanities: 4.5\n568\t    kl50g_retention_avg: 0.54\n569\t    teal30_mtbench_avg: 4.6\n570\t    teal30_retention_avg: 0.72\n571\t  result_rationale: \"MT-Bench 的 multi-turn format 对 sparsity 特别敏感：\\n\\n(1) Turn 2 依赖\\\n572\t    \\ turn 1 的 generation quality — sparsity 引起的 error 会 compound。\\nSparse mask 在\\\n573\t    \\ turn 1 产生的 slight distributional shift 在 turn 2 被 amplified，\\n因为 turn 2 的 prompt\\\n574\t    \\ 包含 turn 1 的（degraded）output。\\n\\n(2) Category-dependent sensitivity：Math/Coding\\\n575\t    \\ 需要 precise symbolic reasoning，\\n对 individual neuron importance 最敏感。Writing/Roleplay\\\n576\t    \\ 更依赖 learned patterns \\n和 fluency，对 mask 的 approximate correctness 更 tolerant。\\n\\\n577\t    Extraction tasks 主要需要 copying relevant content，对 model capacity 要求最低。\\n\\n(3) KL\\\n578\t    \\ 30% retention 81% vs TEAL 30% 72%：KL advantage (+9pp retention) 在 \\nmulti-turn\\\n579\t    \\ 下比 single-task benchmark 更明显，因为 better mask quality 在 \\ncompound error 下的 advantage\\\n580\t    \\ 被放大。\\n\\n(4) GPT-4o judge 倾向于给 fluent but wrong answers 较高分数，\\n这可能 slightly overestimate\\\n581\t    \\ sparse model quality（尤其 Math/Coding categories \\nwhere correctness matters more\\\n582\t    \\ than fluency）。\\n\"\n583\t  tables:\n584\t  - 'Table A6: MT-Bench scores by category'\n585\t  figures_description:\n586\t  - 'Radar chart: 8 MT-Bench categories × 3 conditions (dense, KL 30%, TEAL 30%),\n587\t    showing category-dependent sparsity sensitivity.'\n588\t  analysis: 'MT-Bench 在 median tier 下是 P2 priority，可能不在 main paper 而在 appendix。\n589\t\n590\t    如果包含，key message：KL 30% retains 81% of dense MT-Bench quality，\n591\t\n592\t    但 Math/Coding categories 下降最大（需要 precise reasoning 的 task 对 sparsity 最敏感）。\n593\t\n594\t    如时间不够或 judge API 有 budget 限制，可 defer 到 camera-ready。\n595\t\n596\t    '\n597\t- name: RULER synthetic long-context tasks\n598\t  plan_id: plan_012\n599\t  description: 'RULER at 4K and 16K, 3 representative task types (needle-in-haystack,\n600\t    multi-key,\n601\t\n602\t    multi-value). Fine-grained capability diagnostics.\n603\t\n604\t    '\n605\t  expected_results:\n606\t    dense_4k_needle: 0.95\n607\t    dense_4k_multikey: 0.82\n608\t    dense_4k_multivalue: 0.78\n609\t    dense_16k_needle: 0.88\n610\t    dense_16k_multikey: 0.65\n611\t    dense_16k_multivalue: 0.58\n612\t    kl30u_4k_needle: 0.82\n613\t    kl30u_4k_multikey: 0.6\n614\t    kl30u_4k_multivalue: 0.55\n615\t    kl30u_16k_needle: 0.58\n616\t    kl30u_16k_multikey: 0.32\n617\t    kl30u_16k_multivalue: 0.28\n618\t    kl50g_4k_needle: 0.55\n619\t    kl50g_4k_multikey: 0.3\n620\t    kl50g_4k_multivalue: 0.22\n621\t    kl50g_16k_needle: 0.25\n622\t    kl50g_16k_multikey: 0.12\n623\t    kl50g_16k_multivalue: 0.1\n624\t    teal30_4k_needle: 0.75\n625\t    teal30_4k_multikey: 0.52\n626\t    teal30_4k_multivalue: 0.48\n627\t  result_rationale: \"RULER tasks 的 synthetic nature 使得 sparsity impact 更清晰：\\n\\nNeedle-in-haystack:\\\n628\t    \\ 最 robust（只需找到一个 specific fact），但仍因 sparsity \\n导致 attention 和 FFN 的 interaction\\\n629\t    \\ 退化。4K→16K 下降因为 more distractor tokens。\\n\\nMulti-key/Multi-value: 需要同时 track\\\n630\t    \\ multiple pieces of information，\\n对 model capacity 要求更高。Sparsity 削减的 neurons\\\n631\t    \\ 可能包含 \\\"memory slots\\\"\\n用于 track different keys/values，导致 disproportionate degradation。\\n\\\n632\t    \\nKL 30% vs TEAL 30% on needle@4K: 82% vs 75%。KL's better mask preserves \\nthe\\\n633\t    \\ critical neurons for attention-FFN interaction that retrieval depends on。\\n\\n\\\n634\t    16K 下所有 sparse conditions 显著退化：predictor 在 2048 上训练，\\n16K 的 hidden state distribution\\\n635\t    \\ 偏移更大，compounding with retrieval task difficulty。\\n\"\n636\t  tables:\n637\t  - 'Table A7: RULER synthetic evaluation'\n638\t  figures_description:\n639\t  - 'Heatmap: task type × context length × condition, showing double degradation (sparsity\n640\t    + length).'\n641\t  analysis: \"RULER 作为 P2 experiment，主要作为 LongBench 的 fine-grained diagnostic complement。\\n\\\n642\t    Key finding: sparsity 对 multi-hop retrieval (multikey/multivalue) 的影响远大于 \\nsingle-fact\\\n643\t    \\ retrieval (needle)，providing mechanistic insight into which \\nmodel capabilities\\\n644\t    \\ are most fragile under sparsity。\\n如 LongBench 失败，RULER 可作为 backup long-context\\\n645\t    \\ evidence。\\n\"\n646\t- name: 'C1 causal ablation: BCE trained on KL-derived oracle masks'\n647\t  plan_id: c1_ablation_bce_kl_targets\n648\t  description: 'The headline experiment for Claim 1. BCE predictor trained to match\n649\t    KL-derived\n650\t\n651\t    binary oracle masks (not magnitude oracles). Evaluated at 50% TEAL uniform protocol.\n652\t\n653\t    Tests whether target quality or gradient coupling drives KL advantage.\n654\t\n655\t    In median tier: >95% but not 100% of KL advantage explained by targets.\n656\t\n657\t    '\n658\t  expected_results:\n659\t    c1_s42_ppl: 12.11\n660\t    c1_s42_kl_ref_ppl: 11.96\n661\t    c1_s42_delta: 0.15\n662\t    c1_s42_arc_c: 0.305\n663\t    c1_s42_wg: 0.61\n664\t    c1_s42_mmlu: 0.275\n665\t    c1_s42_gsm8k: 0.017\n666\t    c1_s123_ppl: 12.17\n667\t    c1_s123_kl_ref_ppl: 11.89\n668\t    c1_s123_delta: 0.28\n669\t    c1_s123_arc_c: 0.35\n670\t    c1_s123_wg: 0.605\n671\t    c1_s123_mmlu: 0.27\n672\t    c1_s123_gsm8k: 0.019\n673\t    c1_mean_ppl_delta: 0.22\n674\t    c1_gradient_coupling_contribution_pct: 1.4\n675\t    c1_target_quality_explains_pct: 98.6\n676\t    c1_s42_max_downstream_delta_pp: 2.1\n677\t    c1_s42_max_delta_task: ARC-c\n678\t    c1_s123_max_downstream_delta_pp: 2.9\n679\t    c1_s123_max_delta_task: ARC-c\n680\t    kl_uniform_50_ppl_s42: 11.96\n681\t    bce_magnitude_50_ppl: 27.97\n682\t    mask_divergence_kl_vs_magnitude: 0.53\n683\t    oracle_agreement_c1_predictor: 0.975\n684\t  result_rationale: \"Median tier C1: PPL delta 0.15-0.28，说明 gradient coupling 有 marginal\\\n685\t    \\ non-zero \\ncontribution 但不改变 practical conclusion。\\n\\n为什么 delta > 0（gradient\\\n686\t    \\ coupling ≠ 0）：\\nKL 的 coupled gradient (dL_KL/ds_j depends on ALL active neurons\\\n687\t    \\ via dlogits/dh · dh/dm) \\n让 predictor 在 training 过程中探索 joint neuron interaction\\\n688\t    \\ patterns。BCE 即使给了 \\nKL-derived oracle targets，仍然用 factorized gradient (dL_BCE/ds_j\\\n689\t    \\ depends only on j) \\n来学习。Factorized gradient 无法完全 reproduce KL predictor 学到的\\\n690\t    \\ nuanced scoring —\\n某些 neuron pairs 的 joint importance 只在 coupled gradient 下可见。\\n\\\n691\t    \\n为什么 delta 很小（<0.3 PPL）：\\nOracle masks 提供了 explicit supervision（\\\"keep these\\\n692\t    \\ specific neurons\\\"），\\n大幅减少了 learning complexity。BCE with explicit targets 不需要\\\n693\t    \\ discover importance —\\n只需 classify known-important vs known-unimportant。98.6%\\\n694\t    \\ 的 advantage 来自 knowing \\nWHICH neurons to keep，gradient coupling 只在 edge cases（importance\\\n695\t    \\ scores 接近 threshold \\n的 neurons）有 marginal effect。\\n\\n为什么 ARC-c delta 最大（2.1-2.9pp）：\\n\\\n696\t    ARC-c 的 multi-step reasoning 依赖 specific neuron combinations（\\\"reasoning chains\\\"\\\n697\t    \\ \\nmapped to neuron subsets）。Gradient coupling 使 KL predictor 学到了这些 combinatorial\\\n698\t    \\ \\nimportance patterns，BCE predictor 即使有 oracle targets 也只学到 individual importance。\\n\\\n699\t    在 reasoning tasks 上，neuron combination 的质量差异被放大为 accuracy gap。\\n\\nWinoGrande delta\\\n700\t    \\ 较小（1.4pp）因为 commonsense 更依赖 distributed representations \\n而非 specific neuron\\\n701\t    \\ chains。MMLU/GSM8K 在 50% sparsity 下已 collapse 到 near-random，\\ndelta 被 floor effect\\\n702\t    \\ 掩盖。\\n\"\n703\t  tables:\n704\t  - 'Table 3: C1 Causal Ablation — BCE+KL-targets vs KL'\n705\t  figures_description:\n706\t  - 'Bar chart: PPL comparison — BCE(magnitude) vs BCE+KL-targets vs KL — showing\n707\t    97% gap closure from mask quality alone.'\n708\t  - 'Per-task downstream delta chart: showing ARC-c as the most gradient-coupling-sensitive\n709\t    task.'\n710\t  analysis: \"C1 在 median tier 下需要 nuanced framing：\\n\\nHeadline: \\\"Target quality accounts\\\n711\t    \\ for >95% of KL advantage; gradient coupling \\ncontributes ~1-3% on PPL and up\\\n712\t    \\ to 2.9pp on reasoning tasks.\\\"\\n\\nClaim 1 revision: 从 \\\"sole driver\\\" 改为 \\\"\\\n713\t    dominant driver (>95%)\\\"。\\n保留 \\\"mask pattern discovery\\\" 叙事：53% divergence from\\\n714\t    \\ magnitude oracles 仍是 \\nheadline finding。但 gradient coupling 的 marginal contribution\\\n715\t    \\ 需要 acknowledged。\\n\\nPer-task analysis section (§4.4.1): 解释 ARC-c 对 gradient\\\n716\t    \\ coupling 更敏感，\\n原因是 multi-step reasoning 放大了 neuron combination quality 的差异。\\n\\\n717\t    \\nPractical implication 不变：BCE+KL-targets 仍然需要先训练 KL predictor 来 generate \\noracle\\\n718\t    \\ masks，所以 deployment 时直接用 KL predictor 更简单。C1 的价值是 \\nscientific understanding（why\\\n719\t    \\ KL works），不是 practical pipeline 替代。\\n\"\n720\t- name: Dense sparsity sweep — 6-point regime curve\n721\t  plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n722\t  description: 'KL predictors evaluated at 25%/30%/35%/40%/45%/50% sparsity.\n723\t\n724\t    6-point PPL curve for regime boundary identification.\n725\t\n726\t    '\n727\t  expected_results:\n728\t    kl_25_ppl: 8.2\n729\t    kl_30_ppl: 8.82\n730\t    kl_35_ppl: 9.4\n731\t    kl_40_ppl: 10.12\n732\t    kl_45_ppl: 10.78\n733\t    kl_50_ppl: 11.8\n734\t    delta_25_30: 0.62\n735\t    delta_30_35: 0.58\n736\t    delta_35_40: 0.72\n737\t    delta_40_45: 0.66\n738\t    delta_45_50: 1.02\n739\t    monotonic: true\n740\t    monotonicity_violations: 0\n741\t    noise_band_35pct: 0.2\n742\t    noise_band_note: 35% 在 different seeds 下可能波动 ±0.2 PPL (9.20-9.60)\n743\t    budget_surplus_regime: ≤30%\n744\t    transition_regime: 35%-40%\n745\t    capacity_cliff_onset: 45%-50%\n746\t    acceleration_45_50: delta jumps from 0.66 to 1.02, signaling cliff onset\n747\t  result_rationale: \"6-point curve 在 median tier 下基本单调，但 increments 不 uniform：\\n\\n\\\n748\t    25%→30% (+0.62): 线性区域。每 5pp sparsity 增加 ~0.6 PPL。\\n足够的 neuron budget 使 KL mask\\\n749\t    \\ quality 能完全 absorb 额外 pruning。\\n\\n30%→35% (+0.58): 仍在线性区。但这个 point 有 ±0.2 noise（single\\\n750\t    \\ seed），\\n因为 35% 正处在 budget-surplus → transition 的边界。\\n不同 seeds 的 per-layer allocation\\\n751\t    \\ 在此 sparsity 下 divergence 开始增加。\\n\\n35%→40% (+0.72): increment 开始扩大。Transition\\\n752\t    \\ regime 开始——\\n某些 layers 的 neuron budget 变得 tight，per-layer importance 的 tail\\\n753\t    \\ 被截断。\\n\\n40%→45% (+0.66): 看似 increment 缩小，但因为 40% 用了 global allocation \\n而 45%\\\n754\t    \\ 也是 global，实际 allocation efficiency 在 compensate capacity loss。\\n\\n45%→50% (+1.02):\\\n755\t    \\ 最大 increment。Capacity cliff 开始——critical neuron sets \\n被 pruned 的概率急剧上升。PPL\\\n756\t    \\ 对 pruning 的 sensitivity 非线性增加，\\n因为 remaining neurons 的 marginal importance 更高（已经\\\n757\t    \\ prune 了 all \\\"easy\\\" neurons）。\\n\\n总体 curve shape: 接近 piecewise linear with inflection\\\n758\t    \\ at ~40%，\\n然后 super-linear growth to 50%。不是 smooth quadratic，\\n而是 approximate\\\n759\t    \\ phase transition — 在 median 下 inflection 不够 sharp \\nto call it \\\"phase transition\\\"\\\n760\t    ，改为 \\\"approximate regime boundary\\\"。\\n\"\n761\t  tables:\n762\t  - 'Table 4: 6-point sparsity regime data'\n763\t  figures_description:\n764\t  - 6-point PPL vs sparsity curve with error bars at 35% (±0.2). Dashed vertical lines\n765\t    at 30% and 45% marking regime boundaries. Shaded regions for three regimes.\n766\t  analysis: \"在 median 下 Claim 3 需 calibrate：\\n- \\\"Phase transition\\\" 改为 \\\"approximate\\\n767\t    \\ phase transition\\\"\\n- 35% point 的 noise (±0.2 PPL) 意味着 exact boundary 有 uncertainty\\n\\\n768\t    - 但 overall trend 成立：PPL increase accelerates from ~0.6/5pp to ~1.0/5pp\\n- 与 downstream\\\n769\t    \\ data 交叉验证：downstream 是 strictly monotonic degradation，\\n  进一步支持 regime 叙事（PPL\\\n770\t    \\ 非线性 + downstream 单调 = capacity cliff）\\n- Practical deployment guideline 不变：30%\\\n771\t    \\ 是 sweet spot，40% 需 learned allocation\\n\"\n772\t- name: BCE 30% forced TEAL top-k at recommended operating point\n773\t  plan_id: bce_30pct_forced_topk\n774\t  description: 'BCE predictor evaluated at 30% sparsity via forced TEAL top-k allocation.\n775\t\n776\t    Fills Table 2 gap for BCE at recommended operating point.\n777\t\n778\t    '\n779\t  expected_results:\n780\t    bce_30_forced_topk_ppl: 10.0\n781\t    teal_30_baseline_ppl: 10.97\n782\t    kl_30_uniform_ppl: 8.82\n783\t    bce_30_vs_teal_30_delta: -0.97\n784\t    bce_30_vs_kl_30_delta: 1.18\n785\t    bce_30_arc_c: 0.41\n786\t    bce_30_wg: 0.652\n787\t    bce_30_mmlu: 0.37\n788\t    bce_30_gsm8k: 0.072\n789\t    dense_ppl: 6.12\n790\t    bce_30_ppl_ratio_vs_dense: 1.63\n791\t    kl_30_ppl_ratio_vs_dense: 1.44\n792\t  result_rationale: \"Median tier BCE 30% PPL = 10.0（好于 TEAL 10.97 但差于 KL 8.82）：\\n\\n\\\n793\t    BCE predictor 学到的 scoring 在 30% 下比 50% 更有效，因为：\\n(1) 30% 只需区分 \\\"top 70% important\\\"\\\n794\t    \\ vs \\\"bottom 30% unimportant\\\"，\\n这个 binary classification 相对容易，即使 factorized\\\n795\t    \\ gradient 也能部分学到\\n(2) TEAL forced top-k 在 30% 下给 BCE 一个 reasonable allocation\\\n796\t    \\ baseline，\\nBCE 只需 refine magnitude-based scoring 的 ranking，不需要 fully discover\\\n797\t    \\ importance\\n(3) 30% 的 margin of error 更大——即使 rank 错误一些 neurons，\\n70% kept neurons\\\n798\t    \\ 足以覆盖 most important ones\\n\\n为什么 KL 仍然更好 (8.82 vs 10.0, gap 1.18)：\\nKL 的 coupled\\\n799\t    \\ gradient 在 30% 下仍然比 BCE 学到更好的 neuron ranking，\\n特别是在 borderline neurons (importance\\\n800\t    \\ rank 65-75 percentile) 上。\\n这些 borderline neurons 的正确 inclusion/exclusion 对 PPL\\\n801\t    \\ 有 measurable impact。\\n\\nGap 缩小（1.18 at 30% vs 16.19 at 50%）因为 30% 是 \\\"easier\\\"\\\n802\t    \\ problem —\\nless pruning → less room for mask quality to matter → less KL advantage。\\n\\\n803\t    这与 sparsity sweep 的 finding 一致：KL advantage grows with sparsity。\\n\\nDownstream\\\n804\t    \\ at 30%: BCE 表现 intermediate between TEAL and KL on most tasks，\\nMMLU 37.0% slightly\\\n805\t    \\ below TEAL 38.6%（因为 BCE mask 对 knowledge-relevant \\nneurons 的 coverage 不如 TEAL's\\\n806\t    \\ pure magnitude approach at 30%）。\\n\"\n807\t  tables:\n808\t  - 'Table 2: BCE 30% row completing the comparison table'\n809\t  figures_description:\n810\t  - 'Added to Pareto frontier: BCE 30% point between TEAL 30% and KL 30%, showing\n811\t    KL still dominates.'\n812\t  analysis: \"BCE 30% 在 median 下 gap 从 50% 的 16.19 缩小到 30% 的 1.18，\\n需要 honest reporting：\\n\\\n813\t    \\n- KL 仍优（8.82 vs 10.0），但 margin 更小\\n- Pareto narrative 需调整：强调 KL 在 ALL operating\\\n814\t    \\ points 上 Pareto-dominate BCE，\\n  but gap 是 sparsity-dependent\\n- BCE 30% 优于\\\n815\t    \\ TEAL 30%（10.0 vs 10.97），说明 learned scoring (even factorized) \\n  比 pure magnitude\\\n816\t    \\ 好\\n- Three-tier hierarchy 仍然成立：magnitude (TEAL 10.97) < learned-factorized (BCE\\\n817\t    \\ 10.0) < \\n  learned-coupled (KL 8.82)\\n- 这个 three-tier 结果 strengthens \\\"gradient\\\n818\t    \\ coupling matters\\\" narrative \\n  即使 C1 shows target quality is dominant\"\n819\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20b0e106-df0c-43c4-9dfa-fa82e00c09d1","uuid":"072b8676-91d3-45bd-a49e-d88305df7a7e","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:29:34.774Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_14/projects/distill_sparse_swiglu/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T173518/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Claims 需要 calibration。Claim 1 从 \"sole driver\" 降级为 \"dominant driver\n  (>95%)\"，\n\n  承认 gradient coupling 有 marginal contribution (~3-5%) 但不改变 practical conclusion。\n\n  C1 表述改为 \"BCE+KL-targets recovers >95% of KL advantage\"，不再用 exact match。\n\n  ARC-c 出现 2-3pp delta，需补充 per-task analysis 解释 reasoning tasks 对 gradient pathway\n  更敏感。\n\n  BCE 30% forced top-k PPL 降至 ~10.0（gap 缩小至 1.2 vs KL 8.82），\n\n  需强化 Pareto frontier 叙事：KL 在 quality-efficiency tradeoff 上仍优但 margin 更小，honest reporting。\n\n  6-point regime curve 基本单调，35% 区间有 ±0.2 noise（单次测量），\n\n  改为 \"approximate phase transition\" 并讨论 single-seed noise source。\n\n  仍冲 EMNLP Main，预期 reviewer avg 3.5-4.0，需 minor revision。\n\n  1-2 位审稿人仍有 incremental concern，但多数认为 empirical contribution sufficient。\n\n  关键防御：C1 causal ablation + 53% mask divergence 是 genuine empirical finding，\n\n  不是 engineering trick。14B MMLU gap 作为 honest limitation 报告。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Four-condition ablation @ 50% sparsity\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 'Core comparison: KL-only vs BCE-only vs BCE+comp vs KL+comp at 50%\n    model-level sparsity.\n\n    KL-only (5 seeds) as headline, BCE+comp (5 seeds) as primary competitor,\n\n    KL+comp and BCE-only (3 seeds each) as secondary.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    kl_only_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 9.19\n    kl_only_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.04\n    kl_only_hard_mask_ppl_seeds:\n    - 9.21\n    - 9.25\n    - 9.14\n    - 9.19\n    - 9.15\n    kl_only_teal_global_ppl_mean: 11.78\n    kl_only_teal_global_ppl_std: 0.05\n    kl_only_sparsity: 0.498\n    bce_only_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 28.16\n    bce_only_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.21\n    bce_only_teal_global_ppl_mean: 44.05\n    bce_only_sparsity: 0.496\n    bce_comp_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 20.8\n    bce_comp_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.7\n    bce_comp_teal_global_ppl_mean: 25.5\n    bce_comp_compensation_params: 67248128\n    bce_comp_compensation_params_mb: 256\n    bce_comp_recovery_vs_bce_ppl: 2.5\n    kl_comp_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 9.18\n    kl_comp_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.04\n    kl_comp_teal_global_ppl_mean: 11.78\n    kl_comp_recovery_vs_kl_ppl: 0.01\n    kl_comp_compensation_redundant: true\n  result_rationale: \"KL-only 5-seed consistency (std 0.04) 源于 KL loss 的 output-distribution\\\n    \\ supervision \\n为 predictor 提供了强且稳定的梯度信号（SNR ~5.8x BCE）。所有 seeds 收敛到相似的 mask pattern\\n\\\n    因为 KL landscape 有唯一的 well-defined minimum（neuron importance 由 output distribution\\\n    \\ \\n唯一确定）。\\n\\nBCE-only PPL ~28 是因为 BCE 的 factorized gradient 只能学 per-neuron importance，\\n\\\n    无法捕获 neuron interaction patterns。F1 vs magnitude oracle = 0.61 看似不错，\\n但 functional\\\n    \\ quality 差，因为 the wrong 39% neurons 被错误处理。\\n\\nBCE+comp PPL ~20.8 说明 compensation\\\n    \\ MLP 能部分修复 BCE 的 mask error，\\n但不能替代 mask quality 本身。67.2M 参数（256MB）只换来 ~7 PPL\\\n    \\ improvement，\\n且 KL-only 无需 compensation 就已 PPL 9.19，说明 correct mask > brute-force\\\n    \\ compensation。\\n\\nKL+comp ≈ KL-only 因为 KL mask 已经接近 optimal（留下的 neuron set 正是\\\n    \\ \\noutput distribution preservation 所需），compensation 无残余 error 可修复。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1: Main 4-condition PPL comparison @ 50% sparsity'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: KL-only vs BCE+comp vs TEAL/WINA baselines, PPL on y-axis, conditions\n    on x-axis. Error bars from multi-seed. Key message: KL-only (no comp) outperforms\n    BCE+comp (with 256MB overhead).'\n  analysis: \"Headline: KL-only (PPL 9.19) > BCE+comp (PPL 20.8) by 2.26x, 同时省去 67.2M\\\n    \\ compensation 参数。\\nKL+comp ≈ KL-only 证明 compensation 在 KL 训练下完全冗余。\\nBCE+comp\\\n    \\ 虽优于 BCE-only (20.8 vs 28.16)，但改善仅 7.4 PPL — compensation 是 BCE 的 patch \\n而非根本解决方案。KL\\\n    \\ 对 predictor training 的改进是 structural 的（从 mask quality 层面），\\n不是 compensation\\\n    \\ 能弥补的。\\n\"\n- name: STE baseline (KL + Straight-Through Estimator)\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 'KL loss + STE instead of Gumbel-sigmoid. Isolates loss function vs\n    relaxation method contribution.\n\n    3 seeds.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    ste_hard_mask_ppl_s42: 8.18\n    ste_hard_mask_ppl_s123: 8.25\n    ste_hard_mask_ppl_s456: 8.2\n    ste_hard_mask_ppl_mean: 8.21\n    ste_hard_mask_ppl_std: 0.04\n    ste_sparsity: 0.47\n    ste_sparsity_note: Lagrangian slightly weaker, converges to 47% vs target 50%\n    kl_gumbel_ppl_at_same_sparsity: 9.19\n    ste_vs_gumbel_delta: -1.01\n  result_rationale: \"STE PPL 8.18-8.25 < KL Gumbel PPL 9.19，但 STE sparsity 只达 47%\\\n    \\ vs Gumbel 的 50%。\\nLower sparsity 意味着 STE 保留了更多 neurons（实际是更宽松的 task），所以 PPL\\\n    \\ advantage \\n部分来自 lower effective sparsity。核心结论不变：KL loss（无论用 Gumbel 还是 STE 做\\\n    \\ relaxation）\\n都远优于 BCE loss (28.16)，证明 KL loss function 是 advantage 的 primary\\\n    \\ source，\\nGumbel relaxation 只影响 sparsity convergence 效率（不影响 mask quality）。\\n\\\n    STE Lagrangian 更弱因为 STE gradient 是 biased estimator，导致 sparsity constraint \\n\\\n    learning 较慢。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table A2: Relaxation method ablation (STE vs Gumbel-sigmoid)'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: \"STE 实验确认 KL advantage 来自 loss function 而非 relaxation method。\\nGumbel-sigmoid\\\n    \\ 提供 lower-variance gradient estimates → better Lagrangian convergence → \\nsparsity\\\n    \\ 更准确到达 target。但 mask quality 由 KL loss 的 coupled gradient 决定，\\n与 relaxation 无关。Paper\\\n    \\ 中作为 \\\"R3 concern: Gumbel explains gain\\\" 的直接反驳。\\n\"\n- name: Iso-compute BCE vs KL\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 'BCE training extended to 2700 steps (2.71x KL FLOPs) to rule out compute\n    advantage.\n\n    3 seeds (s42/s123/s456).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_s42: 27.97\n    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_s123: 28.06\n    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_s456: 28.35\n    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_mean: 28.13\n    bce_isocompute_teal_ppl_std: 0.2\n    bce_isocompute_training_steps: 2700\n    bce_isocompute_flops_ratio_vs_kl: 2.71\n    kl_1000step_ppl: 11.78\n    bce_loss_saturation_step: 500\n    bce_loss_500_to_2700_delta: 0.006\n  result_rationale: \"BCE loss 在 ~500 steps 后饱和（final loss 0.638 → 0.632，delta 仅 0.006），\\n\\\n    额外 2200 steps 几乎无改善。这证明 BCE-KL gap 是 structural mismatch 而非 compute deficit。\\n\\\n    BCE 的 factorized gradient (dL/ds_j depends only on neuron j) 意味着 learning landscape\\\n    \\ \\n存在 fundamental limit — 无论多少 compute 都无法让 BCE 学到 neuron interaction patterns。\\n\\\n    2.71x FLOPs → PPL 28.13 vs KL 11.78 (2.39x gap)，confirmed structural explanation。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table A3: Iso-compute comparison'\n  figures_description:\n  - BCE loss curve showing saturation at ~500 steps, with arrow marking KL equivalent\n    compute point.\n  analysis: '完全排除 \"KL wins only because more compute\" concern。\n\n    BCE loss saturation at step 500 意味着 BCE predictor 已到达其 expressiveness limit —\n\n    即使 compute 无限也无法学到 KL-quality masks。\n\n    Gap 2.39x 在 iso-compute 下与 standard compute 下几乎相同 (2.38x)，\n\n    证明额外 compute 对 BCE 无帮助。\n\n    '\n- name: SPON reimplementation on Llama 3.1 8B\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 'Learnable bias vectors + KL training for static correction.\n\n    Recovery rate and interference with dense model.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    spon_sparse_ppl: 8.991\n    kl_pred_ppl_no_spon: 9.217\n    spon_recovery_pct: 7.3\n    spon_ppl_improvement: 0.226\n    dense_with_spon_ppl: 6.182\n    dense_ppl_degradation: 0.065\n    mean_bias_norm: 0.053\n    trainable_params: 458752\n    trainable_pct_of_model: 0.0057\n    teal_with_spon_ppl: 11.79\n    teal_without_spon_ppl: 12.08\n    teal_spon_recovery_pct: 4.8\n  result_rationale: \"SPON 的 static bias correction 只能修复 input-independent 的 systematic\\\n    \\ error。\\nRecovery 7.3% 说明 KL predictor 的 residual error 中只有一小部分是 static bias\\\n    \\ —\\n大部分 error 是 per-input adaptive 的（取决于 specific token context 下的 neuron importance）。\\n\\\n    Dense PPL degradation 0.065 (6.12 → 6.18) 说明 SPON bias 会轻微干扰 dense forward pass，\\n\\\n    因为 bias 是为 sparse activation pattern 优化的，在 dense 下是 noise。\\nSPON 对 TEAL baseline\\\n    \\ 的 recovery (4.8%) 更低，因为 TEAL 的 error 更分散（per-layer \\nmagnitude 误差），static correction\\\n    \\ 更无效。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table A1: SPON analysis — recovery rate and dense degradation'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: \"SPON recovery 仅 7.3% 直接支撑 Claim 2：static correction 太弱，无法 complement\\\n    \\ KL。\\n同时，SPON 的 dense degradation (0.065 PPL) 意味着实际 net benefit 更小。\\nConclusion:\\\n    \\ SPON addresses the wrong error component — KL's residual is dominated by \\n\\\n    per-input adaptive errors that static bias cannot fix。\\n\"\n- name: SPON subsumption logit-space analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Output-space decomposition: linearity test, magnitude ratio, cosine\n    similarity.\n\n    Per-layer orthogonality analysis. 50 samples × 2048 tokens.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    linearity_ratio: 0.264\n    linearity_ratio_std: 0.007\n    magnitude_ratio_spon_vs_kl: 0.158\n    magnitude_ratio_std: 0.009\n    cosine_similarity_mean: 0.196\n    cosine_similarity_std: 0.027\n    kl_predictor_effect_norm: 482.65\n    spon_correction_norm: 76.2\n    interaction_norm: 147.74\n    per_layer_cosine_max: 0.0\n    conclusion_type: weak_subsumption\n  result_rationale: \"Cosine similarity 0.196 (接近 orthogonal，远低于 0.5) 证明 SPON correction\\\n    \\ 和 KL predictor \\neffect 作用在 logit space 的几乎正交方向。Magnitude ratio 15.8% 说明即使 SPON\\\n    \\ 和 KL \\n方向一致，SPON 的修正幅度也只有 KL 的 1/6。\\nPer-layer cosine ≤ 0 (所有层) 意味着在每一层 SPON\\\n    \\ 要么和 KL 正交要么轻微反向。\\nInteraction term 147.74 (30.6% of KL effect) 看似不小，但这是 nonlinear\\\n    \\ cross-layer \\ninteraction — SPON bias 会改变 subsequent layers 的 input distribution，\\n\\\n    但这种 interaction 并不 translate to PPL improvement（SPON recovery 仅 7.3%）。\\nConclusion:\\\n    \\ SPON 和 KL 靶向不同的 error components，且 SPON 的 component 太弱，\\ncomposition 无实际收益。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table A1: SPON subsumption metrics'\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-layer cosine similarity heatmap showing near-zero or negative values across\n    all 32 layers.\n  analysis: 'Logit-space decomposition 提供 Claim 2 的 mechanistic explanation：\n\n    KL 的 coupled gradient 学到的 mask pattern 在 output space 产生 large-magnitude correction\n    (482.65)，\n\n    SPON 的 static bias 产生 small near-orthogonal correction (76.2)。\n\n    两者靶向的 error mode 不同（per-input vs static），\n\n    SPON 的 mode 太弱无法 complement KL。\n\n    '\n- name: Training-free baselines (TEAL, WINA, R-Sparse)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'TEAL (magnitude + greedy), WINA (weight-informed), R-Sparse (rank-aware)\n    at 30%/50%/70%.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    teal_global_ppl_30: 10.97\n    teal_global_ppl_50: 23.31\n    teal_global_ppl_70: 100.11\n    wina_global_ppl_30: 11.45\n    wina_global_ppl_50: 27.93\n    wina_global_ppl_70: 137.24\n    rsparse_global_ppl_50: 151.2\n    dense_ppl: 6.12\n    teal_greedy_allocation_ppl_50: 33.47\n  result_rationale: \"Training-free methods 的 PPL 随 sparsity 急剧增长（TEAL 30%→50%→70%:\\\n    \\ 10.97→23.31→100.11），\\n因为 magnitude-based pruning 在 high sparsity 下 increasingly\\\n    \\ 删除 functionally important neurons。\\nTEAL > WINA > R-Sparse 因为 TEAL 的 global\\\n    \\ allocation 比 WINA 的 weight-informed scoring \\n更有效地分配 per-layer sparsity budget。R-Sparse\\\n    \\ 的 rank-aware scoring 在 SwiGLU architecture \\n上表现最差，因为 SwiGLU 的 gating mechanism\\\n    \\ 使得 rank-based importance 不可靠。\\nTEAL greedy allocation (33.47) 远差于 global (23.31)，说明\\\n    \\ allocation strategy \\n对 training-free methods 同样重要。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1: Training-free baselines row in main comparison table'\n  figures_description:\n  - PPL vs sparsity curve for all training-free methods, showing exponential degradation.\n  analysis: \"三层 hierarchy 成立：training-free (TEAL 10.97-100.11) < static-learned (SPON)\\\n    \\ < \\ncontextual-learned (KL 8.82-11.78)。\\nTEAL 作为 strongest training-free baseline\\\n    \\ 仍比 KL 30% 差 2.15 PPL (10.97 vs 8.82)。\\nAt 50%, gap expands to 11.53 PPL (23.31\\\n    \\ vs 11.78)。\\nNon-linear gap expansion 说明 learned contextual prediction 在 high\\\n    \\ sparsity 下 advantage 更大。\\n\"\n- name: Full benchmark evaluation + Pareto frontier\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'WikiText-2 PPL + 4 downstream tasks (ARC-c, WinoGrande, MMLU, GSM8K)\n    across all conditions.\n\n    Wall-clock profiling. Efficiency-accuracy Pareto frontier.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dense_ppl: 6.12\n    dense_arc_c: 0.583\n    dense_wg: 0.781\n    dense_mmlu: 0.653\n    dense_gsm8k: 0.488\n    kl30u_ppl_mean: 8.82\n    kl30u_ppl_std: 0.01\n    kl30u_arc_c_mean: 0.443\n    kl30u_arc_c_std: 0.032\n    kl30u_wg_mean: 0.692\n    kl30u_wg_std: 0.006\n    kl30u_mmlu_mean: 0.385\n    kl30u_mmlu_std: 0.018\n    kl30u_gsm8k_mean: 0.072\n    kl30u_gsm8k_std: 0.002\n    kl50g_ppl_mean: 11.78\n    kl50g_arc_c_mean: 0.343\n    kl50g_wg_mean: 0.631\n    kl50g_mmlu_mean: 0.281\n    kl50g_gsm8k_mean: 0.021\n    teal30_ppl: 10.97\n    teal30_arc_c: 0.423\n    teal30_wg: 0.661\n    teal30_mmlu: 0.386\n    teal30_gsm8k: 0.079\n    teal50_ppl: 23.31\n    teal50_arc_c: 0.284\n    teal50_wg: 0.53\n    teal50_mmlu: 0.283\n    teal50_gsm8k: 0.011\n    bce_iso_teal_ppl_mean: 28.13\n    bce_iso_arc_c_mean: 0.265\n    bce_iso_wg_mean: 0.518\n    bce_iso_mmlu_mean: 0.261\n    bce_iso_gsm8k_mean: 0.021\n    dense_latency_ms: 119.1\n    kl30_latency_ms: 126.6\n    kl50_latency_ms: 126.8\n    predictor_overhead_ms: 3.17\n    predictor_overhead_pct: 2.7\n    theoretical_flops_speedup_30pct: 1.36\n    theoretical_flops_speedup_50pct: 2.45\n    actual_wallclock_speedup_30pct: 0.94\n    no_sparse_kernel_note: No wall-clock speedup without custom sparse GEMV kernels\n  result_rationale: \"KL 30% uniform 是 recommended operating point 的 median-tier 表现：\\n\\\n    - PPL: 8.82 vs TEAL 10.97 (−19.6%)，KL clearly wins\\n- MMLU: 38.5% vs TEAL 38.6%\\\n    \\ — essentially tied. Median 下 MMLU advantage 被 seed variance (std 1.8%) 淹没\\n\\\n    - WinoGrande: 69.2% vs 66.1% — KL wins by +3.1pp，超过 noise margin\\n- ARC-c: 44.3%\\\n    \\ vs 42.3% — KL slightly better (+2.0pp) 但 seed std 3.2% 使得 significance 不确定\\n\\\n    - GSM8K: 7.2% vs 7.9% — TEAL slightly better by 0.7pp，within noise\\n\\nDownstream\\\n    \\ advantage 不如 PPL advantage 一致，因为 discriminative tasks 对 specific \\nneuron subsets\\\n    \\ 敏感（不同 seed 的 mask 在 critical task-relevant neurons 上有差异）。\\nPPL 是 average over\\\n    \\ all tokens，对 mask quality 更敏感也更稳定。\\n\\nLatency: 无 wall-clock speedup 因为 standard\\\n    \\ PyTorch 不支持 structured sparse GEMV。\\nPredictor overhead 2.7% (3.17ms/119.1ms)\\\n    \\ 在 sparse kernel 可用时可被 sparsity savings \\n(theoretical 1.36x at 30%) 覆盖。Paper\\\n    \\ 报告 theoretical FLOPs savings + overhead。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 2: Downstream benchmarks across all conditions'\n  - 'Table 6: Latency profiling and efficiency analysis'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Pareto frontier: x-axis = theoretical FLOPs (or predictor params), y-axis = WikiText-2\n    PPL. KL 30% uniform dominates the frontier. TEAL/WINA/BCE on suboptimal side.'\n  - 'Radar chart or grouped bar: downstream task retention (% of dense) by condition.'\n  analysis: \"Pareto frontier 叙事在 median 下需 calibration：\\n- PPL: KL clearly dominates\\\n    \\ (−19.6% at 30%)\\n- Downstream: mixed. KL 30% uniform beats TEAL on WG (+3.1pp)\\\n    \\ and ARC-c (+2.0pp)，\\n  但 MMLU 平局且 GSM8K 略输 (−0.7pp)\\n- Honest framing: \\\"KL\\\n    \\ dominates PPL frontier and provides comparable-to-better downstream,\\n  with\\\n    \\ advantage concentrated on WG and ARC-c; GSM8K within noise\\\"\\n- Latency limitation:\\\n    \\ 需 custom sparse kernels 才能实现 wall-clock speedup。\\n  Report theoretical FLOPs\\\n    \\ + predictor overhead，acknowledge practical speedup pending。\\n\"\n- name: Sparsity regime analysis (30%/40%/50%/70%)\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'KL-only at 30%/50%/70% + intermediate points (40%). Test scaling trend.\n\n    Combined with dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt for 6-point curve.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    kl_30_uniform_ppl: 8.82\n    kl_30_uniform_mmlu: 0.406\n    kl_40_global_ppl: 10.12\n    kl_40_global_mmlu: 0.381\n    kl_50_global_ppl: 11.78\n    kl_50_global_mmlu: 0.281\n    kl_50_uniform_ppl: 11.94\n    kl_50_uniform_mmlu: 0.278\n    kl_70_global_ppl: 17.91\n    kl_70_downstream_collapsed: true\n    teal_30_ppl: 10.97\n    teal_50_ppl: 23.31\n    teal_70_ppl: 100.11\n    kl_teal_gap_30: 2.15\n    kl_teal_gap_50: 11.53\n    kl_teal_gap_70: 82.2\n    regime_budget_surplus_boundary: 0.3\n    regime_capacity_cliff_boundary: 0.5\n    ppl_nonmonotonicity: 40% PPL (8.36) < 30% PPL (8.82) under uniform allocation\n      (non-monotonic)\n    downstream_strictly_monotonic: true\n  result_rationale: \"三个 regime 的 mechanistic explanation：\\n\\n(1) Budget-surplus (≤30%):\\\n    \\ 每层都有充足的 neuron budget，uniform allocation 消除 \\nlayer starvation（σ_MMLU 从 9.5pp\\\n    \\ 降到 1.3pp）。KL mask quality 优势最大化，\\n因为 abundant budget 允许 KL 选择 truly important\\\n    \\ neurons 而非被迫 compromise。\\n\\n(2) Budget-constrained (~40%): uniform 反而不如 global（MMLU\\\n    \\ 30.7% vs 38.1%）。\\n当 budget 紧张时，learned per-layer allocation (global topk) 比\\\n    \\ blind uniformity \\n更能将有限 budget 分配给 critical layers。这是 non-monotonic allocation\\\n    \\ preference \\n的机制原因。\\n\\n(3) Capacity-cliff (≥50%): 模型 capacity 本身不足，无论如何分配都 collapse。\\n\\\n    MMLU ≈ 28% ≈ random（4-choice）。KL 仍能维持 PPL 11.78，因为 PPL 是 continuous metric \\n\\\n    更 robust to partial capacity loss，而 MMLU 需要 discrete reasoning chain 完整。\\n\\nPPL\\\n    \\ non-monotonicity (40% < 30% under uniform): 因为 40% 用了 global allocation \\n(10.12)\\\n    \\ 而 30% 用了 uniform (8.82)，但如果比较 30% global (8.98) vs 40% global (10.12)，\\nPPL\\\n    \\ 仍然单调递增。Non-monotonicity 只在 cross-allocation comparison 下出现。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 4: Three-regime sparsity analysis'\n  figures_description:\n  - PPL vs sparsity curve (KL vs TEAL) showing diverging gap at high sparsity.\n  - 'Downstream task retention heatmap: tasks × sparsity levels, color = % of dense.'\n  analysis: 'Regime analysis 的 median narrative：三个 regime 存在且 boundaries 明确，\n\n    non-monotonic allocation preference 是 genuine finding。\n\n    Practical recommendation: 30% sparsity + uniform allocation for deployment。\n\n    KL gap over TEAL grows nonlinearly (2.15 → 11.53 → 82.20)，\n\n    说明 learned contextual prediction 的 value 随 sparsity 急剧增加。\n\n    '\n- name: Mistral-7B-v0.3 cross-architecture validation\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 'KL-only at 30%/50%/70% on Mistral-7B-v0.3 (GQA + sliding window attention).\n\n    Validates that KL advantage transfers across architectures.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mistral_dense_ppl: 5.52\n    mistral_dense_arc_c: 0.602\n    mistral_dense_wg: 0.787\n    mistral_dense_mmlu: 0.624\n    mistral_dense_gsm8k: 0.365\n    mistral_kl30_teal_ppl: 6.77\n    mistral_kl30_ppl_ratio: 1.23\n    mistral_kl50_teal_ppl: 8.65\n    mistral_kl50_arc_c: 0.318\n    mistral_kl50_wg: 0.629\n    mistral_kl50_mmlu: 0.23\n    mistral_kl50_gsm8k: 0.021\n    mistral_kl50_mmlu_retention: 0.368\n    mistral_kl70_teal_ppl: 13.33\n    mistral_teal30_ppl: 8.38\n    mistral_teal50_ppl: 18.31\n    mistral_teal70_ppl: 61.72\n    mistral_kl_teal_ratio_30: 1.24\n    mistral_kl_teal_ratio_50: 2.12\n    mistral_kl_teal_ratio_70: 4.63\n    llama_kl_teal_ratio_30: 1.24\n    llama_kl_teal_ratio_50: 1.98\n    llama_kl_teal_ratio_70: 5.59\n    cross_arch_ratio_consistent: true\n  result_rationale: \"KL advantage ratio (KL_teal / TEAL) 在 Mistral 上与 Llama 高度一致：\\n\\\n    30%: 1.24 vs 1.24, 50%: 2.12 vs 1.98, 70%: 4.63 vs 5.59。\\n这说明 KL distillation\\\n    \\ 的 advantage 来自 SwiGLU architecture 的通用特性\\n（coupled gradient captures neuron\\\n    \\ interaction patterns），而非 specific model weights。\\n\\nMistral 的 GQA + sliding\\\n    \\ window attention 不影响 FFN sparsity prediction，\\n因为 predictor 只在 FFN block 内操作（input\\\n    \\ = hidden state after attention）。\\nAttention mechanism 差异只影响 hidden state distribution，不改变\\\n    \\ KL vs BCE 的 \\nfundamental learning dynamics。\\n\\nDownstream 在 50%: MMLU 23.0%\\\n    \\ 同样 collapse 到 near-random，\\n与 Llama 的 28.1% 一致（both ≈ random 25%）。\\n这 cross-validates\\\n    \\ capacity cliff 存在于 both architectures。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 5: Cross-architecture generalization (Mistral-7B)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'KL/TEAL PPL ratio comparison: Llama vs Mistral at 30%/50%/70%, showing consistent\n    advantage.'\n  analysis: 'Cross-architecture validation 成功：KL advantage ratio 在 Mistral 上 preserved。\n\n    GSM8K 的 catastrophic drop (36.5% dense → 2.1% KL 50%) 在 Mistral 上更严重，\n\n    可能因为 Mistral 的 math capability 本身较弱 (36.5% vs Llama''s 48.8%)。\n\n    Limitation: 仍是 7-8B scale，14B (Qwen) 已知有 MMLU disconnect。\n\n    '\n- name: LongBench English subset evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 'LongBench English subset (4K-32K tokens). KL-only, BCE, TEAL, SPON\n    conditions.\n\n    Per-task-type breakdown. Tests predictor generalization beyond 2048 training length.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dense_narrativeqa: 18.2\n    dense_qasper: 27.5\n    dense_hotpotqa: 25.8\n    dense_gov_report: 30.0\n    dense_multi_news: 25.1\n    dense_triviaqa: 82.0\n    kl30u_narrativeqa: 12.5\n    kl30u_qasper: 19.8\n    kl30u_hotpotqa: 15.2\n    kl30u_gov_report: 22.1\n    kl30u_multi_news: 17.5\n    kl30u_triviaqa: 56.8\n    kl30u_avg_retention: 0.64\n    kl50g_narrativeqa: 6.2\n    kl50g_qasper: 10.8\n    kl50g_hotpotqa: 7.5\n    kl50g_gov_report: 14.2\n    kl50g_multi_news: 9.1\n    kl50g_triviaqa: 32.5\n    kl50g_avg_retention: 0.35\n    teal30_narrativeqa: 10.8\n    teal30_qasper: 17.2\n    teal30_hotpotqa: 13.0\n    teal30_gov_report: 19.5\n    teal30_multi_news: 14.8\n    teal30_triviaqa: 50.2\n    teal30_avg_retention: 0.56\n    kl30u_retention_4k: 0.72\n    kl30u_retention_8k: 0.63\n    kl30u_retention_16k: 0.52\n    kl30u_retention_32k: 0.41\n    length_degradation_note: Predictor trained on 2048 tokens; generalization degrades\n      with context length\n  result_rationale: \"Predictor 在 2048 token 上训练，对 longer context 的 generalization\\\n    \\ 有 length-dependent degradation。\\n原因：neuron importance distribution 随 context\\\n    \\ length 变化——longer context 中 attention pattern\\n更 distributed，导致 hidden state\\\n    \\ 的 distributional shift。Predictor 学到的 importance pattern \\n基于 short-context hidden\\\n    \\ states，在 long-context 下 partially misaligned。\\n\\nKL 30% 平均 retention 64% 优于\\\n    \\ TEAL 30% 的 56%，说明 KL mask quality advantage 在 \\nlong-context 下 preserved（虽然\\\n    \\ absolute performance 下降）。\\n\\nPer-task-type pattern: extraction tasks (TriviaQA,\\\n    \\ HotpotQA) 受 sparsity 影响较小，\\ngeneration tasks (NarrativeQA, MultiNews) 影响较大——generation\\\n    \\ 需要更完整的 capacity \\n来 maintain fluency and coherence over long outputs。\\n\\nSummarization\\\n    \\ (GovReport) intermediate: 需要 comprehension (robust) + generation (fragile)。\\n\\\n    \\nInfrastructure 风险：基于 registry 中多次 LongBench 失败 (v1-v5)，median 预期 \\n只有部分 tasks\\\n    \\ 产出可靠结果，可能需要 partial reporting。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table A5: LongBench results (English subset)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Retention vs context length curve: showing degradation from 4K to 32K for KL\n    30% vs TEAL 30%.'\n  analysis: 'LongBench 在 median tier 下提供 mixed evidence：\n\n    - KL > TEAL on all task types（advantage preserved）\n\n    - 但 absolute retention 在 long context 下显著下降（72% at 4K → 41% at 32K for KL 30%）\n\n    - 这 motivates future work on long-context-aware predictor training\n\n    - Paper 中作为 partial success + honest limitation 报告。\n\n    - Infrastructure issues 可能导致只报告 subset of tasks。\n\n    '\n- name: MT-Bench multi-turn evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: '80 multi-turn questions, 8 categories, GPT-4o judge.\n\n    Tests instruction-following quality under sparsity.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dense_mtbench_avg: 6.35\n    dense_writing: 7.2\n    dense_roleplay: 7.0\n    dense_reasoning: 5.8\n    dense_math: 4.5\n    dense_coding: 5.2\n    dense_extraction: 7.5\n    dense_stem: 6.8\n    dense_humanities: 6.8\n    kl30u_mtbench_avg: 5.15\n    kl30u_writing: 6.0\n    kl30u_roleplay: 5.8\n    kl30u_reasoning: 4.2\n    kl30u_math: 2.8\n    kl30u_coding: 3.5\n    kl30u_extraction: 6.5\n    kl30u_stem: 5.5\n    kl30u_humanities: 5.9\n    kl30u_retention_avg: 0.81\n    kl50g_mtbench_avg: 3.4\n    kl50g_writing: 4.2\n    kl50g_roleplay: 3.8\n    kl50g_reasoning: 2.5\n    kl50g_math: 1.5\n    kl50g_coding: 2.0\n    kl50g_extraction: 5.0\n    kl50g_stem: 3.5\n    kl50g_humanities: 4.5\n    kl50g_retention_avg: 0.54\n    teal30_mtbench_avg: 4.6\n    teal30_retention_avg: 0.72\n  result_rationale: \"MT-Bench 的 multi-turn format 对 sparsity 特别敏感：\\n\\n(1) Turn 2 依赖\\\n    \\ turn 1 的 generation quality — sparsity 引起的 error 会 compound。\\nSparse mask 在\\\n    \\ turn 1 产生的 slight distributional shift 在 turn 2 被 amplified，\\n因为 turn 2 的 prompt\\\n    \\ 包含 turn 1 的（degraded）output。\\n\\n(2) Category-dependent sensitivity：Math/Coding\\\n    \\ 需要 precise symbolic reasoning，\\n对 individual neuron importance 最敏感。Writing/Roleplay\\\n    \\ 更依赖 learned patterns \\n和 fluency，对 mask 的 approximate correctness 更 tolerant。\\n\\\n    Extraction tasks 主要需要 copying relevant content，对 model capacity 要求最低。\\n\\n(3) KL\\\n    \\ 30% retention 81% vs TEAL 30% 72%：KL advantage (+9pp retention) 在 \\nmulti-turn\\\n    \\ 下比 single-task benchmark 更明显，因为 better mask quality 在 \\ncompound error 下的 advantage\\\n    \\ 被放大。\\n\\n(4) GPT-4o judge 倾向于给 fluent but wrong answers 较高分数，\\n这可能 slightly overestimate\\\n    \\ sparse model quality（尤其 Math/Coding categories \\nwhere correctness matters more\\\n    \\ than fluency）。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table A6: MT-Bench scores by category'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart: 8 MT-Bench categories × 3 conditions (dense, KL 30%, TEAL 30%),\n    showing category-dependent sparsity sensitivity.'\n  analysis: 'MT-Bench 在 median tier 下是 P2 priority，可能不在 main paper 而在 appendix。\n\n    如果包含，key message：KL 30% retains 81% of dense MT-Bench quality，\n\n    但 Math/Coding categories 下降最大（需要 precise reasoning 的 task 对 sparsity 最敏感）。\n\n    如时间不够或 judge API 有 budget 限制，可 defer 到 camera-ready。\n\n    '\n- name: RULER synthetic long-context tasks\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 'RULER at 4K and 16K, 3 representative task types (needle-in-haystack,\n    multi-key,\n\n    multi-value). Fine-grained capability diagnostics.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dense_4k_needle: 0.95\n    dense_4k_multikey: 0.82\n    dense_4k_multivalue: 0.78\n    dense_16k_needle: 0.88\n    dense_16k_multikey: 0.65\n    dense_16k_multivalue: 0.58\n    kl30u_4k_needle: 0.82\n    kl30u_4k_multikey: 0.6\n    kl30u_4k_multivalue: 0.55\n    kl30u_16k_needle: 0.58\n    kl30u_16k_multikey: 0.32\n    kl30u_16k_multivalue: 0.28\n    kl50g_4k_needle: 0.55\n    kl50g_4k_multikey: 0.3\n    kl50g_4k_multivalue: 0.22\n    kl50g_16k_needle: 0.25\n    kl50g_16k_multikey: 0.12\n    kl50g_16k_multivalue: 0.1\n    teal30_4k_needle: 0.75\n    teal30_4k_multikey: 0.52\n    teal30_4k_multivalue: 0.48\n  result_rationale: \"RULER tasks 的 synthetic nature 使得 sparsity impact 更清晰：\\n\\nNeedle-in-haystack:\\\n    \\ 最 robust（只需找到一个 specific fact），但仍因 sparsity \\n导致 attention 和 FFN 的 interaction\\\n    \\ 退化。4K→16K 下降因为 more distractor tokens。\\n\\nMulti-key/Multi-value: 需要同时 track\\\n    \\ multiple pieces of information，\\n对 model capacity 要求更高。Sparsity 削减的 neurons\\\n    \\ 可能包含 \\\"memory slots\\\"\\n用于 track different keys/values，导致 disproportionate degradation。\\n\\\n    \\nKL 30% vs TEAL 30% on needle@4K: 82% vs 75%。KL's better mask preserves \\nthe\\\n    \\ critical neurons for attention-FFN interaction that retrieval depends on。\\n\\n\\\n    16K 下所有 sparse conditions 显著退化：predictor 在 2048 上训练，\\n16K 的 hidden state distribution\\\n    \\ 偏移更大，compounding with retrieval task difficulty。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table A7: RULER synthetic evaluation'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: task type × context length × condition, showing double degradation (sparsity\n    + length).'\n  analysis: \"RULER 作为 P2 experiment，主要作为 LongBench 的 fine-grained diagnostic complement。\\n\\\n    Key finding: sparsity 对 multi-hop retrieval (multikey/multivalue) 的影响远大于 \\nsingle-fact\\\n    \\ retrieval (needle)，providing mechanistic insight into which \\nmodel capabilities\\\n    \\ are most fragile under sparsity。\\n如 LongBench 失败，RULER 可作为 backup long-context\\\n    \\ evidence。\\n\"\n- name: 'C1 causal ablation: BCE trained on KL-derived oracle masks'\n  plan_id: c1_ablation_bce_kl_targets\n  description: 'The headline experiment for Claim 1. BCE predictor trained to match\n    KL-derived\n\n    binary oracle masks (not magnitude oracles). Evaluated at 50% TEAL uniform protocol.\n\n    Tests whether target quality or gradient coupling drives KL advantage.\n\n    In median tier: >95% but not 100% of KL advantage explained by targets.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    c1_s42_ppl: 12.11\n    c1_s42_kl_ref_ppl: 11.96\n    c1_s42_delta: 0.15\n    c1_s42_arc_c: 0.305\n    c1_s42_wg: 0.61\n    c1_s42_mmlu: 0.275\n    c1_s42_gsm8k: 0.017\n    c1_s123_ppl: 12.17\n    c1_s123_kl_ref_ppl: 11.89\n    c1_s123_delta: 0.28\n    c1_s123_arc_c: 0.35\n    c1_s123_wg: 0.605\n    c1_s123_mmlu: 0.27\n    c1_s123_gsm8k: 0.019\n    c1_mean_ppl_delta: 0.22\n    c1_gradient_coupling_contribution_pct: 1.4\n    c1_target_quality_explains_pct: 98.6\n    c1_s42_max_downstream_delta_pp: 2.1\n    c1_s42_max_delta_task: ARC-c\n    c1_s123_max_downstream_delta_pp: 2.9\n    c1_s123_max_delta_task: ARC-c\n    kl_uniform_50_ppl_s42: 11.96\n    bce_magnitude_50_ppl: 27.97\n    mask_divergence_kl_vs_magnitude: 0.53\n    oracle_agreement_c1_predictor: 0.975\n  result_rationale: \"Median tier C1: PPL delta 0.15-0.28，说明 gradient coupling 有 marginal\\\n    \\ non-zero \\ncontribution 但不改变 practical conclusion。\\n\\n为什么 delta > 0（gradient\\\n    \\ coupling ≠ 0）：\\nKL 的 coupled gradient (dL_KL/ds_j depends on ALL active neurons\\\n    \\ via dlogits/dh · dh/dm) \\n让 predictor 在 training 过程中探索 joint neuron interaction\\\n    \\ patterns。BCE 即使给了 \\nKL-derived oracle targets，仍然用 factorized gradient (dL_BCE/ds_j\\\n    \\ depends only on j) \\n来学习。Factorized gradient 无法完全 reproduce KL predictor 学到的\\\n    \\ nuanced scoring —\\n某些 neuron pairs 的 joint importance 只在 coupled gradient 下可见。\\n\\\n    \\n为什么 delta 很小（<0.3 PPL）：\\nOracle masks 提供了 explicit supervision（\\\"keep these\\\n    \\ specific neurons\\\"），\\n大幅减少了 learning complexity。BCE with explicit targets 不需要\\\n    \\ discover importance —\\n只需 classify known-important vs known-unimportant。98.6%\\\n    \\ 的 advantage 来自 knowing \\nWHICH neurons to keep，gradient coupling 只在 edge cases（importance\\\n    \\ scores 接近 threshold \\n的 neurons）有 marginal effect。\\n\\n为什么 ARC-c delta 最大（2.1-2.9pp）：\\n\\\n    ARC-c 的 multi-step reasoning 依赖 specific neuron combinations（\\\"reasoning chains\\\"\\\n    \\ \\nmapped to neuron subsets）。Gradient coupling 使 KL predictor 学到了这些 combinatorial\\\n    \\ \\nimportance patterns，BCE predictor 即使有 oracle targets 也只学到 individual importance。\\n\\\n    在 reasoning tasks 上，neuron combination 的质量差异被放大为 accuracy gap。\\n\\nWinoGrande delta\\\n    \\ 较小（1.4pp）因为 commonsense 更依赖 distributed representations \\n而非 specific neuron\\\n    \\ chains。MMLU/GSM8K 在 50% sparsity 下已 collapse 到 near-random，\\ndelta 被 floor effect\\\n    \\ 掩盖。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 3: C1 Causal Ablation — BCE+KL-targets vs KL'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: PPL comparison — BCE(magnitude) vs BCE+KL-targets vs KL — showing\n    97% gap closure from mask quality alone.'\n  - 'Per-task downstream delta chart: showing ARC-c as the most gradient-coupling-sensitive\n    task.'\n  analysis: \"C1 在 median tier 下需要 nuanced framing：\\n\\nHeadline: \\\"Target quality accounts\\\n    \\ for >95% of KL advantage; gradient coupling \\ncontributes ~1-3% on PPL and up\\\n    \\ to 2.9pp on reasoning tasks.\\\"\\n\\nClaim 1 revision: 从 \\\"sole driver\\\" 改为 \\\"\\\n    dominant driver (>95%)\\\"。\\n保留 \\\"mask pattern discovery\\\" 叙事：53% divergence from\\\n    \\ magnitude oracles 仍是 \\nheadline finding。但 gradient coupling 的 marginal contribution\\\n    \\ 需要 acknowledged。\\n\\nPer-task analysis section (§4.4.1): 解释 ARC-c 对 gradient\\\n    \\ coupling 更敏感，\\n原因是 multi-step reasoning 放大了 neuron combination quality 的差异。\\n\\\n    \\nPractical implication 不变：BCE+KL-targets 仍然需要先训练 KL predictor 来 generate \\noracle\\\n    \\ masks，所以 deployment 时直接用 KL predictor 更简单。C1 的价值是 \\nscientific understanding（why\\\n    \\ KL works），不是 practical pipeline 替代。\\n\"\n- name: Dense sparsity sweep — 6-point regime curve\n  plan_id: dense_sparsity_sweep_6pt\n  description: 'KL predictors evaluated at 25%/30%/35%/40%/45%/50% sparsity.\n\n    6-point PPL curve for regime boundary identification.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    kl_25_ppl: 8.2\n    kl_30_ppl: 8.82\n    kl_35_ppl: 9.4\n    kl_40_ppl: 10.12\n    kl_45_ppl: 10.78\n    kl_50_ppl: 11.8\n    delta_25_30: 0.62\n    delta_30_35: 0.58\n    delta_35_40: 0.72\n    delta_40_45: 0.66\n    delta_45_50: 1.02\n    monotonic: true\n    monotonicity_violations: 0\n    noise_band_35pct: 0.2\n    noise_band_note: 35% 在 different seeds 下可能波动 ±0.2 PPL (9.20-9.60)\n    budget_surplus_regime: ≤30%\n    transition_regime: 35%-40%\n    capacity_cliff_onset: 45%-50%\n    acceleration_45_50: delta jumps from 0.66 to 1.02, signaling cliff onset\n  result_rationale: \"6-point curve 在 median tier 下基本单调，但 increments 不 uniform：\\n\\n\\\n    25%→30% (+0.62): 线性区域。每 5pp sparsity 增加 ~0.6 PPL。\\n足够的 neuron budget 使 KL mask\\\n    \\ quality 能完全 absorb 额外 pruning。\\n\\n30%→35% (+0.58): 仍在线性区。但这个 point 有 ±0.2 noise（single\\\n    \\ seed），\\n因为 35% 正处在 budget-surplus → transition 的边界。\\n不同 seeds 的 per-layer allocation\\\n    \\ 在此 sparsity 下 divergence 开始增加。\\n\\n35%→40% (+0.72): increment 开始扩大。Transition\\\n    \\ regime 开始——\\n某些 layers 的 neuron budget 变得 tight，per-layer importance 的 tail\\\n    \\ 被截断。\\n\\n40%→45% (+0.66): 看似 increment 缩小，但因为 40% 用了 global allocation \\n而 45%\\\n    \\ 也是 global，实际 allocation efficiency 在 compensate capacity loss。\\n\\n45%→50% (+1.02):\\\n    \\ 最大 increment。Capacity cliff 开始——critical neuron sets \\n被 pruned 的概率急剧上升。PPL\\\n    \\ 对 pruning 的 sensitivity 非线性增加，\\n因为 remaining neurons 的 marginal importance 更高（已经\\\n    \\ prune 了 all \\\"easy\\\" neurons）。\\n\\n总体 curve shape: 接近 piecewise linear with inflection\\\n    \\ at ~40%，\\n然后 super-linear growth to 50%。不是 smooth quadratic，\\n而是 approximate\\\n    \\ phase transition — 在 median 下 inflection 不够 sharp \\nto call it \\\"phase transition\\\"\\\n    ，改为 \\\"approximate regime boundary\\\"。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 4: 6-point sparsity regime data'\n  figures_description:\n  - 6-point PPL vs sparsity curve with error bars at 35% (±0.2). Dashed vertical lines\n    at 30% and 45% marking regime boundaries. Shaded regions for three regimes.\n  analysis: \"在 median 下 Claim 3 需 calibrate：\\n- \\\"Phase transition\\\" 改为 \\\"approximate\\\n    \\ phase transition\\\"\\n- 35% point 的 noise (±0.2 PPL) 意味着 exact boundary 有 uncertainty\\n\\\n    - 但 overall trend 成立：PPL increase accelerates from ~0.6/5pp to ~1.0/5pp\\n- 与 downstream\\\n    \\ data 交叉验证：downstream 是 strictly monotonic degradation，\\n  进一步支持 regime 叙事（PPL\\\n    \\ 非线性 + downstream 单调 = capacity cliff）\\n- Practical deployment guideline 不变：30%\\\n    \\ 是 sweet spot，40% 需 learned allocation\\n\"\n- name: BCE 30% forced TEAL top-k at recommended operating point\n  plan_id: bce_30pct_forced_topk\n  description: 'BCE predictor evaluated at 30% sparsity via forced TEAL top-k allocation.\n\n    Fills Table 2 gap for BCE at recommended operating point.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bce_30_forced_topk_ppl: 10.0\n    teal_30_baseline_ppl: 10.97\n    kl_30_uniform_ppl: 8.82\n    bce_30_vs_teal_30_delta: -0.97\n    bce_30_vs_kl_30_delta: 1.18\n    bce_30_arc_c: 0.41\n    bce_30_wg: 0.652\n    bce_30_mmlu: 0.37\n    bce_30_gsm8k: 0.072\n    dense_ppl: 6.12\n    bce_30_ppl_ratio_vs_dense: 1.63\n    kl_30_ppl_ratio_vs_dense: 1.44\n  result_rationale: \"Median tier BCE 30% PPL = 10.0（好于 TEAL 10.97 但差于 KL 8.82）：\\n\\n\\\n    BCE predictor 学到的 scoring 在 30% 下比 50% 更有效，因为：\\n(1) 30% 只需区分 \\\"top 70% important\\\"\\\n    \\ vs \\\"bottom 30% unimportant\\\"，\\n这个 binary classification 相对容易，即使 factorized\\\n    \\ gradient 也能部分学到\\n(2) TEAL forced top-k 在 30% 下给 BCE 一个 reasonable allocation\\\n    \\ baseline，\\nBCE 只需 refine magnitude-based scoring 的 ranking，不需要 fully discover\\\n    \\ importance\\n(3) 30% 的 margin of error 更大——即使 rank 错误一些 neurons，\\n70% kept neurons\\\n    \\ 足以覆盖 most important ones\\n\\n为什么 KL 仍然更好 (8.82 vs 10.0, gap 1.18)：\\nKL 的 coupled\\\n    \\ gradient 在 30% 下仍然比 BCE 学到更好的 neuron ranking，\\n特别是在 borderline neurons (importance\\\n    \\ rank 65-75 percentile) 上。\\n这些 borderline neurons 的正确 inclusion/exclusion 对 PPL\\\n    \\ 有 measurable impact。\\n\\nGap 缩小（1.18 at 30% vs 16.19 at 50%）因为 30% 是 \\\"easier\\\"\\\n    \\ problem —\\nless pruning → less room for mask quality to matter → less KL advantage。\\n\\\n    这与 sparsity sweep 的 finding 一致：KL advantage grows with sparsity。\\n\\nDownstream\\\n    \\ at 30%: BCE 表现 intermediate between TEAL and KL on most tasks，\\nMMLU 37.0% slightly\\\n    \\ below TEAL 38.6%（因为 BCE mask 对 knowledge-relevant \\nneurons 的 coverage 不如 TEAL's\\\n    \\ pure magnitude approach at 30%）。\\n\"\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 2: BCE 30% row completing the comparison table'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Added to Pareto frontier: BCE 30% point between TEAL 30% and KL 30%, showing\n    KL still dominates.'\n  analysis: \"BCE 30% 在 median 下 gap 从 50% 的 16.19 缩小到 30% 的 1.18，\\n需要 honest reporting：\\n\\\n    \\n- KL 仍优（8.82 vs 10.0），但 margin 更小\\n- Pareto narrative 需调整：强调 KL 在 ALL operating\\\n    \\ points 上 Pareto-dominate BCE，\\n  but gap 是 sparsity-dependent\\n- BCE 30% 优于\\\n    \\ TEAL 30%（10.0 vs 10.97），说明 learned scoring (even factorized) \\n  比 pure magnitude\\\n    \\ 好\\n- Three-tier hierarchy 仍然成立：magnitude (TEAL 10.97) < learned-factorized (BCE\\\n    \\ 10.0) < \\n  learned-coupled (KL 8.82)\\n- 这个 three-tier 结果 strengthens \\\"gradient\\\n    \\ coupling matters\\\" narrative \\n  即使 C1 shows target quality is dominant\"\n","numLines":819,"startLine":1,"totalLines":819}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019rekv63bcNEpyWwXf9ffTE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper (10 pages) and the review context. Let me summarize what I understand:\n\n**Paper**: \"What Does KL Distillation Learn for SwiGLU Sparsity Prediction? Mask Pattern Discovery Beyond Magnitude Oracles\"\n\n**Core claims**:\n1. KL-trained masks diverge 53% from magnitude oracles, discovering a fundamentally different neuron importance landscape\n2. Target quality (not gradient coupling) is the dominant driver (>95%) of KL's advantage\n3. Three sparsity regimes exist (budget-surplus ≤30%, budget-constrained ~40%, capacity-cliff ≥50%)\n\n\n4. KL eliminates the need for compensation networks\n\nThe paper backs these claims with a comprehensive experimental suite—I'm seeing the ablation studies, baseline comparisons, and full benchmarks all mapped to their corresponding tables and sections throughout the work.\n\nNow I'm ready to assign reviewers: one to scrutinize the methods and experimental rigor, another to evaluate the novelty and positioning relative to existing work.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31164,"cache_read_input_tokens":25058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31164},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20b0e106-df0c-43c4-9dfa-fa82e00c09d1","uuid":"2421a077-432e-48d4-8dd8-63aeb1ec81dd"}
