{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V6nYer8W8CPQDciZuYxvZ9","type":"tool_result","content":"paper/related_work.tex:5:CATS~\\cite{lee2024cats} adapts per-layer thresholds for SiLU/SwiGLU activations; R-Sparse~\\cite{zhang2025rsparse} predicts sparsity from rank-aware SVD projections; DIP~\\cite{federici2025dip} combines dynamic input pruning with cache-aware masking; SparseInfer~\\cite{shin2025sparseinfer} predicts activation sparsity patterns from attention outputs without additional training.\npaper/experiments.tex:22:We compare against: (1) \\textbf{Vanilla TEAL}~\\cite{liu2025teal}, which uses activation magnitudes directly; (2) \\textbf{BCE predictor} (DejaVu-style~\\cite{liu2023dejavu}), trained with per-neuron binary cross-entropy on magnitude-based oracle masks for 1000 and 2700 steps; (3) \\textbf{Uniform allocation}, which distributes the sparsity budget equally across layers; and (4) \\textbf{WINA}~\\cite{liu2025teal}, an importance-weighted variant.\npaper/references.bib:81:  title = {R-Sparse: Rank-Aware Activation Sparsity for Efficient LLM Inference},"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QSVrioRM1nc2c8wAncaLmD","session_id":"20b0e106-df0c-43c4-9dfa-fa82e00c09d1","uuid":"d047f130-3c36-42fc-8970-d51101ad6e7b","timestamp":"2026-05-18T18:32:07.552Z"}
